WEBVTT

1
00:01:29.452 --> 00:01:35.917
<i>Busan Family Church</i>

2
00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:33.808
Don't have a baby if you'll abandon it.

3
00:02:36.644 --> 00:02:39.022
You follow that woman.

4
00:04:07.277 --> 00:04:08.904
Anyone there?

5
00:04:11.822 --> 00:04:13.908
Must've run off.

6
00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:16.870
I guess so.

7
00:04:17.536 --> 00:04:19.539
Give me a towel.

8
00:04:28.089 --> 00:04:32.343
"Woo-sung, I'm sorry.
I'll come back for you."

9
00:04:33.011 --> 00:04:35.263
Here we go again with "I'll come back".

10
00:04:35.346 --> 00:04:37.223
No phone number.

11
00:04:37.307 --> 00:04:39.517
Woo-sung, I'm sorry.
I'll come back for you.

12
00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.978
No way she comes back.

13
00:04:42.687 --> 00:04:44.981
Erase the video, quick.

14
00:04:53.406 --> 00:04:55.783
Look at those shiny eyes.

15
00:04:55.867 --> 00:05:01.873
Not much for eyebrows,
but still, he's so adorable.

16
00:05:02.165 --> 00:05:05.418
How could anyone throw him away?

17
00:05:07.545 --> 00:05:09.547
So you're Woo-sung?

18
00:05:09.923 --> 00:05:11.632
That's right, Woo-sung.

19
00:05:12.175 --> 00:05:15.887
Let's be happy with us.

20
00:07:12.503 --> 00:07:19.469
BROKER

21
00:07:37.778 --> 00:07:42.993
<i>...passengers taking an
express bus can get off here.</i>

22
00:07:53.628 --> 00:08:00.385
<i>Use exit no. 3 for Busan
Intercity Bus Terminal...</i>

23
00:08:55.231 --> 00:08:57.525
How's the knee? It was hurting before.

24
00:08:57.608 --> 00:08:59.360
- It's fine now.
- It's okay?

25
00:08:59.444 --> 00:09:01.154
It's much better.

26
00:09:02.447 --> 00:09:05.241
Come out often. The exercise will help.

27
00:09:05.325 --> 00:09:08.286
Whenever I get here, I need a rest.

28
00:09:08.619 --> 00:09:10.371
How's the laundry business?

29
00:09:10.455 --> 00:09:13.249
Well, just so-so.

30
00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:33.228
♪ Brother Socrates... ♪

31
00:10:00.463 --> 00:10:02.132
Anyway,

32
00:10:03.341 --> 00:10:08.263
it's pretty bold of them to use a
baby box for human trafficking.

33
00:10:09.639 --> 00:10:12.934
Creating that box in the first place

34
00:10:13.226 --> 00:10:16.062
makes for more irresponsible mothers.

35
00:10:16.354 --> 00:10:19.399
I think you have a hidden nice side.

36
00:10:20.525 --> 00:10:21.609
What?

37
00:10:21.692 --> 00:10:26.072
If you'd left it outside,
it would've died.

38
00:10:28.783 --> 00:10:30.451
I am nice.

39
00:10:30.911 --> 00:10:32.787
Didn't you know?

40
00:10:33.079 --> 00:10:35.748
Was it a boy or a girl?

41
00:10:42.463 --> 00:10:45.008
- Hello!
- Good afternoon!

42
00:10:45.258 --> 00:10:47.593
That was so delicious last time.

43
00:10:47.802 --> 00:10:50.846
What was it called? Schu...

44
00:10:52.598 --> 00:10:53.641
Schweinshaxe.

45
00:10:53.724 --> 00:10:54.851
The day after eating it,

46
00:10:54.935 --> 00:10:57.520
my skin was so shiny,
I couldn't believe it.

47
00:10:57.603 --> 00:10:59.647
Come on, it's just pig trotters.

48
00:10:59.772 --> 00:11:02.150
Have you heard of
<i>choucroute</i> by any chance?

49
00:11:02.275 --> 00:11:06.237
I'm going to try making it,
you're welcome to join us.

50
00:11:06.321 --> 00:11:08.781
It's just pork stew. Pretty bland.

51
00:11:08.907 --> 00:11:12.452
The whites are at the cleaner's,
so I brought black ones.

52
00:11:12.535 --> 00:11:13.244
Nice and thick.

53
00:11:13.328 --> 00:11:14.162
Thanks.

54
00:11:14.245 --> 00:11:15.330
Just in case, you know...

55
00:11:15.413 --> 00:11:16.289
Thanks.

56
00:11:16.372 --> 00:11:17.874
Bye, then.

57
00:11:20.043 --> 00:11:21.752
Have a good day!

58
00:11:25.882 --> 00:11:29.469
Shouldn't you at least step
out of the car, as a courtesy?

59
00:11:29.552 --> 00:11:30.720
No need.

60
00:11:30.803 --> 00:11:34.474
He's at home all day anyway.
This gets him exercise.

61
00:11:35.058 --> 00:11:37.768
He is the ideal type for marriage.

62
00:11:37.853 --> 00:11:39.104
Really?

63
00:11:39.229 --> 00:11:41.231
How so? You want him?

64
00:11:41.481 --> 00:11:43.483
If you ever have a baby,

65
00:11:43.566 --> 00:11:46.152
he'll be home writing
so he can care for it.

66
00:11:48.029 --> 00:11:50.198
The mother came back?

67
00:11:54.744 --> 00:11:56.204
Something odd?

68
00:11:56.621 --> 00:11:57.830
Yeah.

69
00:11:58.456 --> 00:12:01.792
She says she left him outside.
Outside the box.

70
00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.798
Was she just confused in the moment?

71
00:12:12.888 --> 00:12:16.724
If you think she'll call the
cops, bring her here. Okay?

72
00:12:17.475 --> 00:12:19.102
I will.

73
00:12:20.436 --> 00:12:21.897
Yeah.

74
00:12:28.194 --> 00:12:30.864
Nothing's written in our records.

75
00:12:33.116 --> 00:12:34.492
Call the pastor.

76
00:12:34.575 --> 00:12:37.078
And can you wash Su-kyung for me?

77
00:12:37.162 --> 00:12:38.704
Okay.

78
00:12:43.043 --> 00:12:45.461
Dong-soo, you were on duty yesterday?

79
00:12:45.921 --> 00:12:48.298
Yes, I always take Sundays.

80
00:12:48.882 --> 00:12:52.468
Please show the babies
here to this woman.

81
00:12:57.473 --> 00:12:59.767
This is the bigger kids' playroom.

82
00:12:59.851 --> 00:13:02.478
There are 19 children living here.

83
00:13:02.854 --> 00:13:05.606
All thrown away in the baby box.

84
00:13:11.487 --> 00:13:15.700
This one came in last week.
The mom's 15 years old.

85
00:13:17.327 --> 00:13:20.121
This one's mother is from Pakistan.

86
00:13:20.205 --> 00:13:22.623
She was a baby sitter, I heard.

87
00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:25.376
This is it?

88
00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:29.130
For now.

89
00:13:31.299 --> 00:13:33.051
Did you leave a note?

90
00:13:33.426 --> 00:13:35.720
Something with the baby?

91
00:13:37.097 --> 00:13:38.598
Yes.

92
00:13:39.099 --> 00:13:42.560
Your name and number,
were they in the note?

93
00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:47.815
Then even if we find the baby,

94
00:13:48.066 --> 00:13:50.568
there's no proof you're the mother.

95
00:13:51.111 --> 00:13:52.863
What's going on?

96
00:13:53.696 --> 00:13:56.867
She's looking for a baby.
Named Woo-sung.

97
00:13:57.742 --> 00:14:01.371
She said she left a baby
outside the box last night.

98
00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:05.583
If you'd left it inside, our
worker would've gone out

99
00:14:05.708 --> 00:14:07.293
and spoken with you.

100
00:14:07.377 --> 00:14:10.755
Yes, that's what I told her.

101
00:14:52.255 --> 00:14:53.756
Not at all.

102
00:14:55.591 --> 00:14:57.093
Kidnapping?

103
00:14:57.843 --> 00:14:59.720
How can you use that word?

104
00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.722
Am I wrong?

105
00:15:02.557 --> 00:15:04.142
You're the one who threw him away.

106
00:15:04.267 --> 00:15:06.561
No, I left him there!

107
00:15:06.727 --> 00:15:09.480
We're not some kind of pet hotel.

108
00:15:09.814 --> 00:15:13.318
I said in the note I'd come back!

109
00:15:18.364 --> 00:15:23.619
If a note says "I'll come back",
he's taken off the adoption list.

110
00:15:24.079 --> 00:15:26.497
100% chance he goes to an orphanage.

111
00:15:26.789 --> 00:15:28.833
You know what that means?

112
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.920
I'm sure you wrote that
with loving intention,

113
00:15:32.087 --> 00:15:36.049
but it closes off all
future paths for him.

114
00:15:36.841 --> 00:15:38.509
We want...

115
00:15:38.718 --> 00:15:40.011
uh, Woo-sung...

116
00:15:40.095 --> 00:15:44.891
to be rescued from that
kind of dark future.

117
00:15:45.808 --> 00:15:48.436
Rather than grow up in an orphanage,

118
00:15:48.519 --> 00:15:54.860
much better to be in the
care of a loving family.

119
00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.155
It's adoption.

120
00:15:59.697 --> 00:16:01.616
We search for parents to raise him.

121
00:16:02.117 --> 00:16:04.410
You people have no right.

122
00:16:04.494 --> 00:16:06.412
Neither do you, after abandoning him.

123
00:16:06.537 --> 00:16:07.705
This is theft!

124
00:16:07.788 --> 00:16:08.664
Protection.

125
00:16:08.748 --> 00:16:12.043
Of course, we don't have
that right, but still...

126
00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:17.090
Shall we describe it as... benevolence?

127
00:16:18.884 --> 00:16:20.426
Benevolence...

128
00:16:21.261 --> 00:16:23.763
Haven't heard that word in ages.

129
00:16:24.014 --> 00:16:26.682
Parents who are unable
to conceive a child,

130
00:16:26.766 --> 00:16:31.104
and who can't wait for the
lengthy adoption review process,

131
00:16:31.271 --> 00:16:35.984
and a mother who for
reasons she cannot say...

132
00:16:36.692 --> 00:16:38.653
Your name is...?

133
00:16:39.863 --> 00:16:42.240
Sun-ah... Moon Sun-ah.

134
00:16:42.365 --> 00:16:48.579
Miss Sun-ah, think of us as cupids
who will embrace your precious child.

135
00:16:49.247 --> 00:16:53.543
We promise to find the best
parents to raise Woo-sung.

136
00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:56.922
Cupids?

137
00:16:57.547 --> 00:16:59.757
Well, forgive the expression...

138
00:17:00.091 --> 00:17:01.342
How about...

139
00:17:01.426 --> 00:17:04.595
Mr. Stork? Or the Stork
Twins, since there are two of us?

140
00:17:05.554 --> 00:17:11.394
And it's case-by-case, but
there is a modest payment.

141
00:17:12.436 --> 00:17:14.147
Payment?

142
00:17:14.856 --> 00:17:16.649
How much was it?

143
00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:20.444
About 10 million won. For a male child.

144
00:17:20.736 --> 00:17:22.155
Who gets the fee?

145
00:17:22.405 --> 00:17:27.077
You, of course. And we
who arrange the deal...

146
00:17:32.082 --> 00:17:34.042
Benevolence, my ass.

147
00:17:34.876 --> 00:17:37.545
You're just brokers.

148
00:17:39.881 --> 00:17:42.383
You could call it that.

149
00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.017
When do we go?

150
00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.034
That must be the mother, right?

151
00:18:09.535 --> 00:18:11.412
Not sure...

152
00:18:13.915 --> 00:18:16.209
Doesn't look like it.

153
00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.721
Hi, Tae-ho.

154
00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:30.431
What are you...?

155
00:18:31.933 --> 00:18:33.559
Hello.

156
00:18:33.726 --> 00:18:36.312
We're closed today.

157
00:18:36.646 --> 00:18:39.983
Don't know if this will wash out...

158
00:18:42.944 --> 00:18:44.237
This...

159
00:18:45.071 --> 00:18:45.989
This is...

160
00:18:46.072 --> 00:18:48.158
It's blood, obviously.

161
00:18:50.076 --> 00:18:51.786
I'll give it a try.

162
00:18:52.078 --> 00:18:55.874
And about the money, next week...

163
00:18:55.957 --> 00:18:58.877
We're thinking of opening
a fried chicken place, here.

164
00:19:01.587 --> 00:19:03.381
If you can't pay, drop by the casino...

165
00:19:03.464 --> 00:19:05.716
No, I'm never going back there.

166
00:19:06.842 --> 00:19:09.095
Guess you've got options.

167
00:19:09.512 --> 00:19:13.349
Then 50 million by next week.
And clean up that shirt.

168
00:19:13.433 --> 00:19:14.851
Yes.

169
00:19:16.561 --> 00:19:18.146
Good bye.

170
00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:21.566
Hey, Tae-ho.

171
00:19:22.442 --> 00:19:25.528
Since when did you start
working with gangsters?

172
00:19:26.029 --> 00:19:27.613
You nagging me?

173
00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:30.741
Mister, mind your own business.

174
00:19:31.367 --> 00:19:34.579
Weren't you running a
restaurant with your mom?

175
00:19:35.663 --> 00:19:38.374
Wheat noodles make
me want to puke, now.

176
00:19:58.061 --> 00:19:59.855
What's with them?

177
00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.399
Nothing. Came to complain.

178
00:20:04.901 --> 00:20:06.736
Fix this, will you?

179
00:20:06.987 --> 00:20:08.905
There's a trick to it.

180
00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:11.241
Push on the left!

181
00:20:22.668 --> 00:20:24.629
Do we need to take her?

182
00:20:25.046 --> 00:20:28.383
With the mom there, it
looks less suspicious.

183
00:20:29.926 --> 00:20:32.303
Sun-ah! Time to go.

184
00:20:32.803 --> 00:20:36.766
It's all about the money
for her. But 5:5?

185
00:20:36.933 --> 00:20:40.186
You said it. Should
be thirds, at least.

186
00:20:42.688 --> 00:20:46.151
It's 2 1/2 hours to Yeongdeok
on the Gyeongbu Expressway.

187
00:20:46.234 --> 00:20:48.403
So we'll pass Gyeongju
Rest Area at lunchtime.

188
00:20:48.528 --> 00:20:50.530
Let's stop there.

189
00:21:19.559 --> 00:21:21.477
In a car like that,

190
00:21:22.437 --> 00:21:24.522
they won't be driving too far, right?

191
00:21:24.898 --> 00:21:28.276
Probably Ulsan or Pohang?

192
00:21:33.406 --> 00:21:36.993
God, I want to take a shower
and change my clothes.

193
00:21:38.744 --> 00:21:40.288
Remember.

194
00:21:40.371 --> 00:21:44.459
We need to arrest them in the act!

195
00:21:53.051 --> 00:21:57.097
Sun-ah, your hometown is...?

196
00:22:01.267 --> 00:22:03.103
I'm from Busan.

197
00:22:04.062 --> 00:22:08.441
This guy claims Seoul
as his hometown...

198
00:22:08.524 --> 00:22:10.110
Claims?

199
00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:13.654
Then what about you?

200
00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:15.240
Yeosu.

201
00:22:15.323 --> 00:22:17.367
Ah, Yeosu.

202
00:22:18.326 --> 00:22:20.620
All they have there is the gondola.

203
00:22:20.786 --> 00:22:22.330
It's a cable car.

204
00:22:22.455 --> 00:22:26.001
The raw sole there is delicious.
And the gatkimchi...

205
00:22:37.428 --> 00:22:40.390
We went there ages ago to sell a baby.

206
00:22:41.099 --> 00:22:43.101
To those gay guys?

207
00:22:43.601 --> 00:22:45.395
Ah, you're right!

208
00:22:45.603 --> 00:22:47.188
That was Yeosu.

209
00:22:47.898 --> 00:22:49.024
I remember.

210
00:22:49.357 --> 00:22:52.693
Wonder how he's getting on.
Must be in primary school.

211
00:22:52.986 --> 00:22:56.656
♪ The night sea in Yeosu... ♪

212
00:23:00.911 --> 00:23:02.703
Don't say anything dumb.

213
00:23:02.871 --> 00:23:04.205
We'll do the negotiating.

214
00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:08.668
Yes, after all, the
customer comes first.

215
00:23:09.252 --> 00:23:12.505
- Think of them as a client...
- They're here.

216
00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:17.093
Mr. Im Chang-ho?

217
00:23:17.510 --> 00:23:19.012
We're here from Busan...

218
00:23:19.095 --> 00:23:20.805
- Show us the baby.
- Sure.

219
00:23:20.889 --> 00:23:22.557
He just woke up.

220
00:23:23.808 --> 00:23:25.643
Isn't he cute?

221
00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:32.108
Did you use Photoshop, by any chance?

222
00:23:32.192 --> 00:23:33.734
He was cuter in the photo.

223
00:23:33.818 --> 00:23:35.904
It's because he just woke up.

224
00:23:36.112 --> 00:23:39.407
But looking at him now,
his eyebrows are so thin...

225
00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:43.078
Because he's a baby. Usually
his eyes are like this.

226
00:23:43.161 --> 00:23:46.289
He's so cute. Woo-sung, open your eyes!

227
00:23:46.372 --> 00:23:48.083
We'll pay 4 million.

228
00:23:48.166 --> 00:23:50.835
But yesterday you said 10 million won.

229
00:23:50.919 --> 00:23:52.879
4 million is a lot for him.

230
00:23:52.963 --> 00:23:53.713
Sure.

231
00:23:54.464 --> 00:23:56.549
Or we'll pay in installments.
You can do that?

232
00:23:56.632 --> 00:23:58.259
Over 12 months.

233
00:23:59.135 --> 00:24:00.553
I've never heard of
something like this.

234
00:24:00.636 --> 00:24:03.348
We can't accept such sudden conditions.

235
00:24:03.556 --> 00:24:05.516
Who is the father?

236
00:24:07.185 --> 00:24:08.561
His dad?

237
00:24:09.104 --> 00:24:10.355
His dad is...

238
00:24:10.438 --> 00:24:14.109
Don't tell me it was rape
or anything like that.

239
00:24:14.192 --> 00:24:16.819
- If a crime is involved...
- How can you say that?

240
00:24:16.945 --> 00:24:20.406
His mother is right
here, she's so devoted.

241
00:24:20.490 --> 00:24:23.243
Caring for her sick parents...

242
00:24:23.326 --> 00:24:25.245
You son of a bitch!

243
00:24:26.204 --> 00:24:27.873
Son of a bitch?

244
00:24:28.456 --> 00:24:33.128
Don't you look in the mirror?
Going on about his eyebrows,

245
00:24:33.211 --> 00:24:34.295
you stupid bitch.

246
00:24:34.379 --> 00:24:36.965
- Are you crazy?
- What did you call me?

247
00:24:37.048 --> 00:24:38.424
Sun-ah!

248
00:24:40.510 --> 00:24:43.804
How can she be so rude?

249
00:24:44.055 --> 00:24:45.306
Rude?

250
00:24:45.431 --> 00:24:47.475
Sure, I'm fucking rude!

251
00:24:47.600 --> 00:24:49.435
And are you respectful?

252
00:24:49.769 --> 00:24:53.731
Talking shit about someone's
baby, is that fucking respectful?

253
00:24:54.357 --> 00:24:57.944
We drove all the way out to this
hick town and what, 4 million?

254
00:24:58.278 --> 00:25:00.947
Are you fucking kidding me?

255
00:25:01.781 --> 00:25:04.659
I'll never give him to
scumbags like you.

256
00:25:04.951 --> 00:25:09.414
Just fuck off before I
hit you, you beggars.

257
00:25:11.666 --> 00:25:13.293
- Beggars?
- What?

258
00:25:22.552 --> 00:25:23.344
How could...

259
00:25:23.428 --> 00:25:25.221
She called us beggars.

260
00:25:43.823 --> 00:25:47.202
Want some crab? They steam it for you.

261
00:25:50.496 --> 00:25:52.123
That was a bit extreme.

262
00:25:52.498 --> 00:25:54.209
Yes, it was.

263
00:25:54.459 --> 00:25:56.252
My point exactly.

264
00:25:57.587 --> 00:26:00.924
They were customers.
We were negotiating.

265
00:26:01.007 --> 00:26:03.426
Right, they're like customers.

266
00:26:03.509 --> 00:26:06.554
If they weren't I would've
slapped them.

267
00:26:08.348 --> 00:26:11.434
This is how we reach a compromise.

268
00:26:12.685 --> 00:26:16.189
Sure, that kind of attitude
won't accomplish...

269
00:26:16.272 --> 00:26:19.650
We can accomplish something
by finding a better buyer!

270
00:26:21.736 --> 00:26:23.154
She's got a point.

271
00:26:23.238 --> 00:26:26.867
4 million, in installments?
Gimme a break.

272
00:26:30.620 --> 00:26:35.125
What should we do? Go back to Busan?

273
00:26:36.334 --> 00:26:39.337
I guess so. Let's do that.

274
00:26:41.589 --> 00:26:43.716
There are other buyers, right?

275
00:26:47.595 --> 00:26:49.514
- Hello, sir.
- Hi.

276
00:26:49.931 --> 00:26:51.850
So, is there blood?

277
00:26:52.017 --> 00:26:53.018
A bit.

278
00:26:53.101 --> 00:26:54.769
- Candy?
- Thank you, sir.

279
00:26:54.853 --> 00:26:57.105
It's Children's Day tomorrow.

280
00:26:57.188 --> 00:26:59.440
My grandma gave me some holiday cash.

281
00:27:04.279 --> 00:27:06.406
Did you identify him?

282
00:27:08.366 --> 00:27:10.243
We're in the process
of contacting his family.

283
00:27:10.952 --> 00:27:12.328
What's the cause of death?

284
00:27:12.662 --> 00:27:14.956
A heavy blow broke his neck.

285
00:27:15.874 --> 00:27:18.084
My, he's still young.

286
00:27:21.587 --> 00:27:24.174
I hate blood so much.

287
00:27:26.592 --> 00:27:28.719
The view here is killer.

288
00:27:34.767 --> 00:27:36.644
It's a woman...

289
00:27:56.456 --> 00:27:58.499
There must be more, right?

290
00:28:01.211 --> 00:28:04.089
Surely they won't go back to Busan?

291
00:28:04.714 --> 00:28:06.716
That won't do.

292
00:28:11.637 --> 00:28:14.265
- Dong-soo!
- Hi.

293
00:28:15.516 --> 00:28:16.601
Foul play!

294
00:28:16.684 --> 00:28:19.520
That guy's the director.
Third generation.

295
00:28:20.063 --> 00:28:22.023
He looks third generation, right?

296
00:28:22.482 --> 00:28:23.483
Dong-soo!

297
00:28:23.566 --> 00:28:24.734
Dong-soo!

298
00:28:24.817 --> 00:28:25.818
How've you been?

299
00:28:25.902 --> 00:28:27.445
How are you?

300
00:28:27.528 --> 00:28:28.821
Dong-soo, let me show you something.

301
00:28:28.905 --> 00:28:31.699
- Dong-soo!
- It's Dong-soo!

302
00:28:31.782 --> 00:28:34.160
Wow, Dong-soo!

303
00:28:34.244 --> 00:28:36.287
It's really him!

304
00:28:47.257 --> 00:28:48.799
So that's why he wanted to come here.

305
00:28:48.884 --> 00:28:51.469
Why didn't you say you were coming?

306
00:28:51.552 --> 00:28:55.098
Your numbers look down again.

307
00:28:55.640 --> 00:28:58.809
Three kids gone in half a year.

308
00:28:59.227 --> 00:29:02.647
4.5 million less per
month. In subsidies.

309
00:29:02.730 --> 00:29:05.150
You kids go play. Hurry up.

310
00:29:05.733 --> 00:29:08.403
Losing team gets finger flicked, okay?

311
00:29:08.694 --> 00:29:10.238
Go play!

312
00:29:11.865 --> 00:29:13.241
Huh?

313
00:29:14.409 --> 00:29:18.663
He found himself a new wife.

314
00:29:20.916 --> 00:29:22.250
She's so young.

315
00:29:22.333 --> 00:29:24.085
How'd they meet?

316
00:29:24.169 --> 00:29:26.546
One of those dating apps?

317
00:29:26.629 --> 00:29:28.839
Hey you!

318
00:29:30.133 --> 00:29:32.593
You dummy, I told
you not to go in there!

319
00:29:32.969 --> 00:29:34.470
Don't you see those flowers?

320
00:29:34.554 --> 00:29:37.682
- Dong-soo, let's play basketball!
- Okay.

321
00:29:37.765 --> 00:29:39.184
Hurry up!

322
00:29:42.437 --> 00:29:46.024
Sarge, last time you told the chief

323
00:29:46.107 --> 00:29:50.320
the church was in on this
child trafficking case...

324
00:29:50.403 --> 00:29:52.363
And it's true.

325
00:29:52.697 --> 00:29:54.657
The younger one is an employee there.

326
00:29:54.740 --> 00:29:56.367
Part time.

327
00:29:57.077 --> 00:29:58.578
He's an employee.

328
00:29:58.703 --> 00:30:00.621
Even if it's a temp job.

329
00:30:01.331 --> 00:30:04.417
Still, for supposedly
professional brokers,

330
00:30:04.834 --> 00:30:07.420
their actions seem pretty improvised...

331
00:30:10.298 --> 00:30:13.426
You put lukewarm water
in this. Didn't you?

332
00:30:16.012 --> 00:30:18.348
It's because you didn't wait 3 minutes.

333
00:30:19.807 --> 00:30:24.104
If you take money, you're
a professional broker, no?

334
00:30:25.313 --> 00:30:28.108
Technically, but...

335
00:30:29.484 --> 00:30:33.571
Calling it a deep organization
seems a bit overstated.

336
00:30:34.405 --> 00:30:38.952
You hate when that Criminal Affairs
guy calls you "the kid", right?

337
00:30:40.661 --> 00:30:42.622
Give it to me.

338
00:30:46.751 --> 00:30:48.044
Give it.

339
00:30:48.294 --> 00:30:49.462
Yoon-woo!

340
00:30:49.545 --> 00:30:50.463
Yes?

341
00:30:50.546 --> 00:30:52.840
Let Ha-jun use that now.

342
00:30:53.716 --> 00:30:55.635
Hae-jin, that's enough soccer for now!

343
00:30:55.718 --> 00:30:57.470
Five more minutes!

344
00:30:58.846 --> 00:31:01.391
His skills aren't improving any.

345
00:31:06.771 --> 00:31:09.107
You still have that scar.

346
00:31:12.402 --> 00:31:14.946
You were bleeding so much then,

347
00:31:15.280 --> 00:31:17.908
we called the ambulance and everything.

348
00:31:18.699 --> 00:31:23.454
There was a kite in the tree, so I
climbed up but a branch broke...

349
00:31:25.415 --> 00:31:28.793
The only one here who gets
into so much trouble is Young-min.

350
00:31:29.419 --> 00:31:30.962
Young-min?

351
00:31:31.796 --> 00:31:33.173
Ah, Young-min...

352
00:31:34.007 --> 00:31:35.884
He's on the run now.

353
00:31:35.967 --> 00:31:37.593
Again?

354
00:31:39.595 --> 00:31:41.973
Just like the old days.

355
00:31:54.777 --> 00:31:56.321
Haven't heard anything.

356
00:31:56.947 --> 00:31:58.489
Unfortunately.

357
00:32:00.616 --> 00:32:04.204
These days, that's not
the main reason I come.

358
00:32:11.502 --> 00:32:15.966
Well, you can think
of it as a blind date.

359
00:32:16.216 --> 00:32:17.508
Toe!

360
00:32:17.592 --> 00:32:20.261
Then I'll send you a photo.

361
00:32:23.056 --> 00:32:26.517
His eyebrows are a bit lacking.

362
00:32:29.938 --> 00:32:32.732
Let me borrow this a sec.

363
00:32:37.153 --> 00:32:39.030
That'll look ridiculous!

364
00:32:40.406 --> 00:32:43.826
Don't you think he looks more manly?

365
00:32:44.535 --> 00:32:46.872
But why am I your wife?

366
00:32:49.958 --> 00:32:52.043
Dong-soo knows everyone here.

367
00:32:52.127 --> 00:32:53.794
Then say I'm your daughter.

368
00:32:57.298 --> 00:32:59.009
We don't look anything alike.

369
00:32:59.592 --> 00:33:01.427
Hey kid, don't touch.

370
00:33:01.511 --> 00:33:03.263
With your dirty hands.

371
00:33:03.388 --> 00:33:05.140
I said, don't touch!

372
00:33:05.223 --> 00:33:07.267
It's just until we find a buyer.

373
00:33:07.350 --> 00:33:09.060
Why so sensitive?

374
00:33:09.144 --> 00:33:10.811
Don't touch!

375
00:33:11.604 --> 00:33:13.064
Your hands are dirty!

376
00:33:13.273 --> 00:33:15.316
His eyebrows look weird.

377
00:33:22.698 --> 00:33:24.825
Can I be your son?

378
00:33:24.993 --> 00:33:26.494
Why?

379
00:33:27.078 --> 00:33:28.704
I want to play soccer.

380
00:33:28.788 --> 00:33:29.956
Soccer?

381
00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:33.459
And make tons of money
like Son Heung-min.

382
00:33:33.584 --> 00:33:36.754
It hasn't been long since
Woo-sung was born.

383
00:33:37.255 --> 00:33:40.466
Too soon for a second, right?

384
00:33:40.841 --> 00:33:43.469
Right. One's more than enough.

385
00:33:43.887 --> 00:33:46.890
I think it's a reasonable offer.

386
00:33:49.935 --> 00:33:53.438
One kid from here became
a pro soccer player.

387
00:33:53.563 --> 00:33:55.523
Which team was it?

388
00:33:55.648 --> 00:33:57.859
They have striped uniforms.

389
00:33:58.068 --> 00:33:59.485
I don't know.

390
00:33:59.610 --> 00:34:04.740
They say that kids from an
orphanage can succeed,

391
00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:06.492
but 97%...

392
00:34:06.576 --> 00:34:08.328
Pretending to be smart again...

393
00:34:09.412 --> 00:34:11.664
- 3% is high!
- That punk...

394
00:34:12.165 --> 00:34:14.625
Just the word 'orphanage'
gets him all worked up.

395
00:34:14.709 --> 00:34:17.503
What percentage of
people succeed anyway?

396
00:34:20.006 --> 00:34:21.674
Who's that?

397
00:34:22.467 --> 00:34:25.929
Someone ran away. I
guess they caught him.

398
00:34:27.138 --> 00:34:29.724
Dong-soo, I broke your record!

399
00:34:31.392 --> 00:34:33.937
It took 3 days before I was caught.

400
00:34:34.520 --> 00:34:36.147
Are you bragging?

401
00:34:36.231 --> 00:34:39.734
If you consider time
as well as distance...

402
00:34:41.194 --> 00:34:43.029
Good for you, jeez...

403
00:34:43.363 --> 00:34:44.865
Hello?

404
00:34:45.949 --> 00:34:47.700
Yes, I understand.

405
00:34:48.284 --> 00:34:50.328
You're in Uljin, right?

406
00:34:50.453 --> 00:34:51.204
No, it's fine.

407
00:34:51.287 --> 00:34:54.832
- See you tomorrow.
- What happened to your eyebrows?

408
00:34:56.417 --> 00:34:59.212
Here's the seafood stew.

409
00:35:06.344 --> 00:35:09.055
- A coin laundromat...
- This is Si-woo.

410
00:35:09.139 --> 00:35:11.141
I played forward, and
he was midfielder.

411
00:35:11.224 --> 00:35:12.976
...will never sew a button for you.

412
00:35:13.059 --> 00:35:17.480
Back then we had enough
kids for two soccer teams!

413
00:35:17.563 --> 00:35:24.654
They won't shorten pants,
or repair a hole in the knee.

414
00:35:26.531 --> 00:35:29.742
You know that law? About adoption.

415
00:35:30.035 --> 00:35:32.120
The Special Adoption Act.

416
00:35:32.370 --> 00:35:35.623
I was hoping it'd be stricter
about foreign adoptions.

417
00:35:35.706 --> 00:35:39.085
But don't all the kids
want to be adopted?

418
00:35:39.544 --> 00:35:40.962
I dunno...

419
00:35:41.087 --> 00:35:45.008
That kid who likes soccer
was really persistent.

420
00:35:45.091 --> 00:35:46.092
Hae-jin...

421
00:35:46.259 --> 00:35:51.056
It's too late for him. He's 7 already.

422
00:35:51.639 --> 00:35:52.640
He's 8.

423
00:35:52.723 --> 00:35:54.851
Ah, that's too late.

424
00:35:55.268 --> 00:35:56.227
It's late.

425
00:35:56.311 --> 00:36:03.151
You've got to figure
people adopt up to age 6.

426
00:36:03.234 --> 00:36:05.820
He must know it, too.

427
00:36:08.323 --> 00:36:12.493
Some kids don't like it and come back.

428
00:36:12.618 --> 00:36:17.832
That adoptee a while
back, who got abused.

429
00:36:19.500 --> 00:36:21.920
Blood is thicker than water.

430
00:36:22.003 --> 00:36:26.424
And what if a new child is
conceived after they adopt?

431
00:36:27.300 --> 00:36:34.182
Right, the kids here
have all been rejected,

432
00:36:34.265 --> 00:36:36.059
when they were abandoned.

433
00:36:36.184 --> 00:36:38.228
But if it happens again...

434
00:36:38.311 --> 00:36:42.565
I've had nothing but
rejection in my life.

435
00:36:43.316 --> 00:36:47.528
At least get rid of the whistle.
This isn't the military.

436
00:36:47.737 --> 00:36:51.741
Hey, as for me,

437
00:36:52.700 --> 00:36:56.162
I want to be a kind of
father figure to them.

438
00:36:56.246 --> 00:36:57.247
You know?

439
00:36:57.622 --> 00:37:01.417
That's why I do this.

440
00:37:08.424 --> 00:37:10.886
Damn... hide, quickly!

441
00:37:24.024 --> 00:37:29.529
♪ Sleep, my baby ♪

442
00:37:31.114 --> 00:37:37.037
♪ In the front yard, and ♪
♪ in the hill in back, ♪

443
00:37:38.121 --> 00:37:43.584
♪ the birds and the baby lambs ♪

444
00:37:45.086 --> 00:37:50.050
♪ are all sleeping ♪

445
00:38:11.029 --> 00:38:12.822
She sang a song.

446
00:38:13.114 --> 00:38:14.490
What song?

447
00:38:15.450 --> 00:38:17.077
A lullaby.

448
00:38:17.660 --> 00:38:19.412
A lullaby?

449
00:38:24.792 --> 00:38:27.879
This place has everything, it's great.

450
00:38:28.504 --> 00:38:30.798
Let's take it all with us!

451
00:38:31.967 --> 00:38:33.843
Do his ears, like this.

452
00:38:33.927 --> 00:38:35.553
You sure talk a lot.

453
00:38:37.638 --> 00:38:41.101
If we keep looking, we
may find a better buyer.

454
00:38:41.184 --> 00:38:43.561
Let's just go with the Uljin people.

455
00:38:43.644 --> 00:38:45.813
Okay, all done...

456
00:38:46.689 --> 00:38:49.109
Now you're all clean.

457
00:38:49.734 --> 00:38:52.695
Your mommy wants to
say bye-bye so quickly.

458
00:38:54.155 --> 00:38:55.573
We're trying our hardest...

459
00:38:55.656 --> 00:38:58.409
Know how hard it is
raising a baby alone?

460
00:38:58.869 --> 00:39:02.122
Still, that doesn't justify
throwing him away.

461
00:39:02.205 --> 00:39:03.999
Then how do you justify selling him?

462
00:39:04.082 --> 00:39:06.667
Someone threw him away, so we sell him.

463
00:39:06.751 --> 00:39:08.628
Get the order right.

464
00:39:08.711 --> 00:39:12.132
Then you shouldn't have made
that box in the first place.

465
00:39:12.215 --> 00:39:14.134
My thoughts exactly!

466
00:39:14.217 --> 00:39:16.427
They say they're trying to save babies,

467
00:39:16.511 --> 00:39:18.763
but instead they just corrupt mothers.

468
00:39:18.846 --> 00:39:19.931
It's not like that.

469
00:39:20.015 --> 00:39:23.351
Thanks to that box,
Woo-sung is alive and well...

470
00:39:23.601 --> 00:39:27.939
Don't use alcohol wipes
on his face. He's crying!

471
00:39:28.648 --> 00:39:30.691
Oh, sorry...

472
00:39:30.816 --> 00:39:33.236
Among all the mothers who leave notes,

473
00:39:33.319 --> 00:39:35.321
how many do you think really come back?

474
00:39:35.405 --> 00:39:37.157
How would I know?

475
00:39:37.532 --> 00:39:39.700
1 out of 40.

476
00:39:39.784 --> 00:39:42.453
The other 39 are never
heard from again.

477
00:39:42.620 --> 00:39:46.207
Why just blame the mothers?
Say that to the fathers, too!

478
00:39:46.291 --> 00:39:48.626
Then at least leave your
phone number in the note!

479
00:39:48.793 --> 00:39:51.254
It's already the second
time I'm hearing this.

480
00:39:51.421 --> 00:39:53.631
Should I say it again?

481
00:39:53.924 --> 00:39:55.216
I can say it all day.

482
00:39:55.300 --> 00:39:57.260
Who are you to act so superior?

483
00:39:57.343 --> 00:40:01.097
The kids in this dirty orphanage
look up to you, so you're conceited?

484
00:40:01.181 --> 00:40:03.224
Just live here, then.

485
00:40:12.943 --> 00:40:15.111
You cold?

486
00:40:15.320 --> 00:40:20.366
Dong-soo thought his
mom would be 1 out of 40.

487
00:40:20.533 --> 00:40:22.869
Look out by the playground.

488
00:40:23.161 --> 00:40:27.623
See that old gate? That's
where he was abandoned.

489
00:40:27.832 --> 00:40:30.751
With a note that said
"I'll come back for you."

490
00:40:30.835 --> 00:40:34.380
That's why he's so touchy,
try to understand.

491
00:40:44.099 --> 00:40:46.559
I saw Jee-young working here.

492
00:40:47.185 --> 00:40:48.895
She came back.

493
00:40:49.812 --> 00:40:51.940
Not easy to be a singer.

494
00:40:54.567 --> 00:40:57.362
Still, I liked her voice.

495
00:40:58.696 --> 00:41:00.365
3 to 1.

496
00:41:07.413 --> 00:41:11.459
But everyone ends up
finding a place here.

497
00:41:15.463 --> 00:41:17.423
Must be fun.

498
00:41:18.674 --> 00:41:20.385
4 to 1.

499
00:41:22.888 --> 00:41:24.389
Fun?

500
00:41:28.726 --> 00:41:31.687
More fun than living alone.

501
00:41:35.316 --> 00:41:42.323
Still, you should go far, far away.

502
00:41:45.826 --> 00:41:47.495
Far away where?

503
00:41:47.578 --> 00:41:50.165
Far.

504
00:41:50.248 --> 00:41:55.128
You're our hope, our star.

505
00:41:57.130 --> 00:41:59.382
Where do you want me to go?

506
00:41:59.925 --> 00:42:02.052
Anywhere.

507
00:42:02.928 --> 00:42:07.848
If even you end up back
here, it'll be kind of sad.

508
00:43:24.425 --> 00:43:26.136
Good morning.

509
00:43:37.355 --> 00:43:40.233
Woo-sung, this is rain!

510
00:43:40.942 --> 00:43:42.318
Rain.

511
00:43:42.944 --> 00:43:45.071
It's just raindrops.

512
00:43:46.572 --> 00:43:48.241
Same thing.

513
00:44:00.921 --> 00:44:03.214
Sorry about yesterday.

514
00:44:04.424 --> 00:44:06.592
I shouldn't have said that.

515
00:44:08.219 --> 00:44:10.346
What was it you said?

516
00:44:16.061 --> 00:44:18.354
I have this dream sometimes.

517
00:44:21.024 --> 00:44:22.943
It's raining...

518
00:44:25.028 --> 00:44:29.115
The rain washes away everything
I was up to yesterday.

519
00:44:33.954 --> 00:44:36.289
But when I open my eyes,

520
00:44:37.373 --> 00:44:41.044
the rain is still pouring down,

521
00:44:44.881 --> 00:44:47.467
and nothing about me has changed.

522
00:44:48.969 --> 00:44:51.137
Don't you just need an umbrella?

523
00:44:52.931 --> 00:44:54.515
Umbrella?

524
00:44:56.726 --> 00:44:59.562
Yeah, a big one.

525
00:45:01.647 --> 00:45:03.859
Big enough for two people.

526
00:45:15.912 --> 00:45:20.291
Then I want a red one.
With a strawberry pattern.

527
00:45:22.252 --> 00:45:25.338
When I was little, my
friend had one of those.

528
00:45:25.881 --> 00:45:27.757
I was so envious.

529
00:45:30.385 --> 00:45:31.802
You stole it?

530
00:45:32.345 --> 00:45:33.721
Yeah.

531
00:45:33.930 --> 00:45:35.891
I threw it away.

532
00:46:16.556 --> 00:46:18.850
So they're not related by blood?

533
00:46:18.934 --> 00:46:21.311
No. They all call her Mom, but...

534
00:46:21.394 --> 00:46:22.854
All?

535
00:46:23.646 --> 00:46:24.689
You woke me up,

536
00:46:24.772 --> 00:46:27.733
startled the old man so he can't sleep.

537
00:46:27.817 --> 00:46:29.069
What's going on?

538
00:46:29.152 --> 00:46:31.321
The police car came
in, what's happening?

539
00:46:31.404 --> 00:46:33.156
Silence!

540
00:46:33.781 --> 00:46:35.491
Come back here.

541
00:46:35.575 --> 00:46:37.327
Just hold on.

542
00:46:41.456 --> 00:46:43.791
I've never seen that man.

543
00:46:43.917 --> 00:46:45.835
What's this about?

544
00:46:46.252 --> 00:46:49.547
He was murdered, in a hotel. Then...

545
00:46:51.091 --> 00:46:52.968
Look closely.

546
00:46:53.384 --> 00:46:56.012
This was taken by the hotel CCTV.

547
00:46:56.096 --> 00:46:58.348
That woman lives here?

548
00:46:58.806 --> 00:47:02.602
Ye-ji, take the kids over there.

549
00:47:03.061 --> 00:47:06.689
In front of the kids, really...

550
00:47:07.023 --> 00:47:08.859
You, the taller one.

551
00:47:08.942 --> 00:47:10.944
The taller one, just a sec.

552
00:47:12.820 --> 00:47:14.322
Candy?

553
00:47:16.950 --> 00:47:20.245
You can speak freely with me.

554
00:47:21.121 --> 00:47:23.581
This woman lives here, right?

555
00:47:26.292 --> 00:47:28.044
I don't know.

556
00:47:35.927 --> 00:47:37.220
Ma'am.

557
00:47:37.553 --> 00:47:41.266
This is a baby she's carrying, right?

558
00:47:41.682 --> 00:47:46.479
I told her not to give birth.
How could she be a mother?

559
00:47:46.562 --> 00:47:48.231
What did you say?

560
00:47:48.439 --> 00:47:51.776
I said I told her not to have it!

561
00:47:51.860 --> 00:47:55.030
How could she be a mother?

562
00:47:57.032 --> 00:47:58.992
Silence!

563
00:48:01.286 --> 00:48:04.289
Taking kids in and making
them do these things...

564
00:48:04.539 --> 00:48:06.666
Is that a mother?

565
00:48:07.542 --> 00:48:14.007
I just look after girls
who've got nowhere to go.

566
00:48:15.508 --> 00:48:17.052
Murder?

567
00:48:20.346 --> 00:48:22.182
She's a prostitute?

568
00:48:26.602 --> 00:48:28.354
So you're saying,

569
00:48:28.521 --> 00:48:31.607
the baby was keeping
her from running away.

570
00:48:34.903 --> 00:48:39.782
Give me 3 days. I'll
make sure they sell him.

571
00:48:48.875 --> 00:48:50.710
Wow...

572
00:48:52.462 --> 00:48:54.714
If it's murder, Criminal
Affairs will be on it.

573
00:48:54.797 --> 00:48:56.841
They already are.

574
00:48:58.801 --> 00:49:00.720
We'd better set it up.

575
00:49:00.887 --> 00:49:02.347
Set it up?

576
00:49:03.139 --> 00:49:04.765
A buyer.

577
00:49:21.074 --> 00:49:23.994
Dammit. Buyer's not answering.

578
00:49:24.785 --> 00:49:28.539
It's because you sent that
photo with the eyebrows.

579
00:49:29.624 --> 00:49:32.502
How about this one? 20 million.

580
00:49:33.378 --> 00:49:35.463
Twice the market price...

581
00:49:36.047 --> 00:49:37.257
Should we meet them?

582
00:49:37.340 --> 00:49:38.758
Huh? Who?

583
00:49:38.884 --> 00:49:41.136
They own a building, it seems.

584
00:49:42.803 --> 00:49:44.805
How old is the woman?

585
00:49:45.056 --> 00:49:46.182
36

586
00:49:46.266 --> 00:49:48.518
Why, you want someone younger?

587
00:49:49.895 --> 00:49:51.897
No, it's not that.

588
00:49:54.065 --> 00:49:56.817
I've got a bad feeling.

589
00:50:00.238 --> 00:50:03.491
Don't you think it's cheap, though?

590
00:50:05.618 --> 00:50:07.245
10 million won?

591
00:50:09.039 --> 00:50:11.666
The going price for a baby.

592
00:50:12.750 --> 00:50:14.961
And for girls it's only 8 million.

593
00:50:15.045 --> 00:50:16.880
- Sarge...
- Yeah?

594
00:50:17.923 --> 00:50:24.137
- Isn't it illegal to bait people?
- Why 2 million cheaper? So annoying.

595
00:50:26.764 --> 00:50:28.599
What did you ask?

596
00:50:28.683 --> 00:50:33.229
I was taught such evidence
can't be used in court.

597
00:50:36.441 --> 00:50:38.443
The criminal intention
was there from the start.

598
00:50:39.194 --> 00:50:41.196
It's not baiting.

599
00:50:43.198 --> 00:50:45.200
It's providing an opportunity.

600
00:50:45.575 --> 00:50:47.077
An opportunity...

601
00:50:48.995 --> 00:50:51.957
♪ Brother Socrates... ♪

602
00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:54.084
Hey, once we close that deal,

603
00:50:54.167 --> 00:50:56.752
back in Busan, that place...

604
00:50:56.836 --> 00:50:59.172
want to go there?

605
00:50:59.297 --> 00:51:01.507
You want to see Jennifer again?

606
00:51:01.674 --> 00:51:04.010
Go yourself. I'm not
into that kind of thing.

607
00:51:04.094 --> 00:51:05.845
Keep your voice down.

608
00:51:06.262 --> 00:51:10.183
Such a nice topic for
a situation like this.

609
00:51:10.350 --> 00:51:13.311
Just trying to lighten the mood.

610
00:51:13.686 --> 00:51:16.397
During military service,
before going out on a drill...

611
00:51:16.481 --> 00:51:19.150
You never went to the
military. You were in jail.

612
00:51:19.234 --> 00:51:20.360
Neither did you.

613
00:51:20.443 --> 00:51:22.653
With the exemption for orphanage kids.

614
00:51:22.737 --> 00:51:25.531
It's the same exemption
gold medalists get.

615
00:51:26.282 --> 00:51:30.495
♪ What is it with love...? ♪

616
00:51:41.631 --> 00:51:43.341
What's wrong?

617
00:51:47.470 --> 00:51:49.973
Why pull over here?

618
00:51:51.599 --> 00:51:53.601
I'm gonna pee my pants!

619
00:51:54.310 --> 00:51:56.312
I almost peed.

620
00:51:56.897 --> 00:51:58.773
That punk.

621
00:52:10.035 --> 00:52:13.914
I told you I had a bad feeling.

622
00:52:14.664 --> 00:52:17.167
The bad feeling was about this?

623
00:52:26.342 --> 00:52:30.346
The car kept shaking, I
almost peed my pants.

624
00:52:34.642 --> 00:52:36.311
This car is junk.

625
00:52:39.022 --> 00:52:41.816
You're the one who climbed into it.

626
00:52:42.358 --> 00:52:45.445
Mister, can you take me with you?

627
00:52:45.528 --> 00:52:46.947
No.

628
00:52:47.322 --> 00:52:49.074
Everyone will worry.

629
00:52:49.157 --> 00:52:51.826
We'll give you money
to ride a bus home.

630
00:52:51.910 --> 00:52:53.494
No!

631
00:52:57.165 --> 00:53:00.168
Why are you interrupting
our family trip?

632
00:53:00.418 --> 00:53:02.837
I know everything. You're not a family.

633
00:53:02.921 --> 00:53:05.298
You're going to sell Woo-sung.

634
00:53:06.174 --> 00:53:08.676
- How much did you hear?
- All of it.

635
00:53:14.349 --> 00:53:17.727
I'll attach the mic here.

636
00:53:18.436 --> 00:53:23.774
Don't be negative and say
his hair's too thin, and so on.

637
00:53:23.942 --> 00:53:26.903
And don't ask the birth
mother about the father.

638
00:53:26.987 --> 00:53:28.905
Seems there was some issue.

639
00:53:29.739 --> 00:53:32.117
- Have some coffee.
- Thank you very much.

640
00:53:32.283 --> 00:53:33.784
Thank you.

641
00:53:35.703 --> 00:53:38.081
Do they look like they own a building?

642
00:53:39.457 --> 00:53:41.960
Are they too young?

643
00:53:42.418 --> 00:53:44.129
I'm sorry.

644
00:53:44.795 --> 00:53:47.548
No, no need to apologize.

645
00:53:48.091 --> 00:53:53.221
You two are in a de facto marriage,
with no marriage certificate.

646
00:53:54.597 --> 00:53:57.642
- So you can't adopt officially.
- Yes.

647
00:54:01.021 --> 00:54:03.523
Let's say your sperm count is low.

648
00:54:04.315 --> 00:54:05.775
Me?

649
00:54:07.861 --> 00:54:09.905
And hand over the money
quickly. Be natural.

650
00:54:09.988 --> 00:54:12.073
I understand. Low sperm
count, act natural.

651
00:54:12.157 --> 00:54:14.742
Low sperm, give money quickly...

652
00:54:15.535 --> 00:54:19.289
So let's practice your dialogue.

653
00:54:19.372 --> 00:54:21.291
Very well.

654
00:54:22.125 --> 00:54:25.378
And this is the money we prepared.

655
00:54:28.589 --> 00:54:31.551
We've done fertility treatments
for 5 years now,

656
00:54:31.634 --> 00:54:34.345
and both of us are so tired.

657
00:54:34.845 --> 00:54:36.222
Sergeant,

658
00:54:36.306 --> 00:54:38.850
should we mention the
de facto marriage here?

659
00:54:38.934 --> 00:54:42.020
That it's hard for us to
adopt officially and all...

660
00:54:42.103 --> 00:54:44.022
Good! Let's do that.

661
00:54:44.105 --> 00:54:45.606
Thank you.

662
00:54:47.775 --> 00:54:51.821
We'll truly treasure this
baby like our own child.

663
00:54:53.865 --> 00:54:56.617
Shall we take out that 'truly'?

664
00:54:56.701 --> 00:55:00.121
Ah, shall we? Okay, no 'truly'...

665
00:55:00.663 --> 00:55:02.665
We'll treasure truly this baby... no.

666
00:55:02.748 --> 00:55:05.168
We'll treasure our own babies...

667
00:55:05.793 --> 00:55:07.462
- What was it?
- We'll treasure...

668
00:55:07.628 --> 00:55:10.506
We'll treasure our baby...

669
00:55:10.798 --> 00:55:16.429
We'll treasure this baby
like our own child.

670
00:55:31.444 --> 00:55:33.989
Can we name this car
"The Hae-jin Express?"

671
00:55:34.572 --> 00:55:36.282
Whatever you want.

672
00:55:36.366 --> 00:55:37.783
All right!

673
00:55:38.201 --> 00:55:39.995
Was it Jennifer?

674
00:55:40.286 --> 00:55:41.913
Who's Jennifer?

675
00:55:42.455 --> 00:55:44.624
Dong-soo's girlfriend.

676
00:55:46.834 --> 00:55:48.836
Hey, what's written on the ball?

677
00:55:48.920 --> 00:55:51.547
Hae-jin, my name.

678
00:55:51.631 --> 00:55:53.591
The pastor named me.

679
00:55:53.758 --> 00:55:57.888
I guess you like your name.

680
00:55:58.096 --> 00:55:59.430
It's not that.

681
00:55:59.514 --> 00:56:02.225
At the orphanage you
need your name on things.

682
00:56:02.558 --> 00:56:06.271
If someone wants to steal it, a
name won't stop them. Right?

683
00:56:06.354 --> 00:56:08.731
<i>Plate #9388, pull over!</i>

684
00:56:10.984 --> 00:56:13.153
<i>Plate #9388, pull over!</i>

685
00:56:13.236 --> 00:56:16.072
What? I wasn't speeding.

686
00:56:16.239 --> 00:56:17.908
Dammit.

687
00:56:24.830 --> 00:56:26.832
You're my wife...

688
00:56:27.708 --> 00:56:30.753
Then you're a married
couple working at my shop.

689
00:56:30.836 --> 00:56:32.797
Married? No way.

690
00:56:32.923 --> 00:56:33.965
No way.

691
00:56:34.049 --> 00:56:35.425
Then you're relatives.
Distant relatives, okay?

692
00:56:35.508 --> 00:56:37.635
How distant? First cousin? Second?

693
00:56:37.718 --> 00:56:39.387
Good afternoon, sir.

694
00:56:39.470 --> 00:56:40.721
Your license?

695
00:56:40.805 --> 00:56:42.098
Yes, sir.

696
00:56:42.515 --> 00:56:45.393
I wasn't driving very fast...

697
00:56:46.269 --> 00:56:48.104
Mr. Ha Jin-young?

698
00:56:48.271 --> 00:56:49.856
Your rear door is open.

699
00:56:49.940 --> 00:56:52.817
If things fall out the back, it
could cause a big accident.

700
00:56:52.901 --> 00:56:55.028
Oh, I'm sorry.

701
00:56:59.824 --> 00:57:01.576
You on a trip somewhere?

702
00:57:01.701 --> 00:57:04.579
Yes, to Lotte World to
ride the Ferris Wheel!

703
00:57:04.662 --> 00:57:06.456
Wow, you're going far!

704
00:57:06.664 --> 00:57:08.041
Yes, it's a family trip.

705
00:57:08.124 --> 00:57:10.043
But there's no Ferris Wheel there.

706
00:57:10.126 --> 00:57:11.544
Really?

707
00:57:12.128 --> 00:57:15.465
For a Ferris Wheel, you
should go to Wolmido.

708
00:57:15.673 --> 00:57:17.884
Should we go to Wolmido, then?

709
00:57:17.968 --> 00:57:21.471
Ask your dad to take
you on a boat cruise too.

710
00:57:21.554 --> 00:57:22.347
Yeah!

711
00:57:22.430 --> 00:57:24.265
I can't deal with boats.

712
00:57:24.515 --> 00:57:26.392
I get seasick.

713
00:57:26.601 --> 00:57:28.353
- You run a laundry shop?
- Yes.

714
00:57:28.436 --> 00:57:30.730
I brought my shirt to be cleaned,

715
00:57:30.813 --> 00:57:33.316
but the sleeves all
shrunk, why is that?

716
00:57:33.816 --> 00:57:36.736
This should be dry cleaned.
They threw it in the wash.

717
00:57:36.819 --> 00:57:37.445
Really?

718
00:57:37.528 --> 00:57:40.198
Too many amateurs in
laundry shops these days...

719
00:57:40.281 --> 00:57:41.741
- Boss?
- You need to take care with...

720
00:57:41.824 --> 00:57:42.993
Boss!

721
00:57:43.076 --> 00:57:45.078
- Boss!
- I think we need to go...

722
00:57:45.286 --> 00:57:46.287
Well, then...

723
00:57:46.371 --> 00:57:47.163
Your license.

724
00:57:47.247 --> 00:57:48.123
Thank you.

725
00:57:48.206 --> 00:57:49.749
Next time, dry clean!

726
00:57:49.832 --> 00:57:52.377
- All right. Have a good day.
- Yes.

727
00:57:54.254 --> 00:57:56.464
- Wolmido!
- Yes, sir...

728
00:58:08.977 --> 00:58:11.646
<i>- Good afternoon.
- Sorry we're late.</i>

729
00:58:11.729 --> 00:58:12.730
<i>Were you waiting long?</i>

730
00:58:12.813 --> 00:58:15.525
<i>Not at all. We just arrived...</i>

731
00:58:15.608 --> 00:58:17.443
<i>I'm Ha Sang-hyun.
You're Mr. Song Ji-cheol?</i>

732
00:58:17.527 --> 00:58:18.653
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

733
00:58:18.904 --> 00:58:21.031
<i>- And he is Woo-sung?
- Yes.</i>

734
00:58:21.948 --> 00:58:24.034
<i>- Are you his mother?
- Yes.</i>

735
00:58:24.117 --> 00:58:26.827
<i>Can I hold him?</i>

736
00:58:28.079 --> 00:58:29.830
<i>Yes, go ahead.</i>

737
00:58:30.331 --> 00:58:32.250
<i>Oh my.</i>

738
00:58:33.293 --> 00:58:35.420
<i>He touched me! Honey...</i>

739
00:58:35.503 --> 00:58:38.839
<i>With prominent facial
features like his...</i>

740
00:58:41.592 --> 00:58:44.054
<i>You'll raise him properly, right?</i>

741
00:58:44.137 --> 00:58:47.098
<i>Of course. We'll treasure him, truly.</i>

742
00:58:47.182 --> 00:58:51.144
<i>If you have your own child later,
you'll love them the same?</i>

743
00:58:51.394 --> 00:58:52.437
<i>Of course.</i>

744
00:58:52.896 --> 00:58:56.399
Quit talking and give them the cash!

745
00:58:56.482 --> 00:58:57.901
Money money!

746
00:58:57.984 --> 00:59:00.278
<i>Will you keep doing
fertility treatments?</i>

747
00:59:01.196 --> 00:59:04.699
<i>We've tried for 5 years
already. Both of us...</i>

748
00:59:04.782 --> 00:59:07.160
<i>- Both of us are tired.
- Yes.</i>

749
00:59:07.243 --> 00:59:10.496
<i>And since we aren't
officially married...</i>

750
00:59:11.206 --> 00:59:13.458
<i>Did you do an AMH test?</i>

751
00:59:14.042 --> 00:59:16.461
<i>Or an HSG?</i>

752
00:59:17.587 --> 00:59:20.173
<i>Yes... that one.</i>

753
00:59:20.840 --> 00:59:23.301
<i>I guess Letrozole had no effect?</i>

754
00:59:23.426 --> 00:59:26.679
<i>None... and I had bad side
effects with the Letrozole.</i>

755
00:59:26.762 --> 00:59:30.641
<i>It was so hard for me
to see him that way.</i>

756
00:59:31.351 --> 00:59:34.145
<i>Letrozole induces ovulation,</i>

757
00:59:35.021 --> 00:59:37.858
<i>so of course, it won't
have any effect on you.</i>

758
00:59:38.900 --> 00:59:41.444
<i>I mean, my sperm count...</i>

759
00:59:41.611 --> 00:59:44.072
<i>We're talking about ovulation,
what does sperm count matter?</i>

760
00:59:44.155 --> 00:59:46.366
<i>Take this!</i>

761
01:00:02.548 --> 01:00:04.800
They wanted to resell him.

762
01:00:04.926 --> 01:00:06.302
I could tell right away.

763
01:00:06.386 --> 01:00:07.762
Reselling, you know?

764
01:00:07.845 --> 01:00:09.722
Hae-jin, don't open that window.

765
01:00:09.805 --> 01:00:11.933
Someone paid them to act as parents.

766
01:00:12.142 --> 01:00:15.896
How do you know so much
about fertility treatments?

767
01:00:16.521 --> 01:00:20.233
A similar thing happened last
year. Sang-hyun totally fell for it.

768
01:00:20.316 --> 01:00:21.401
Hands off!

769
01:00:21.484 --> 01:00:23.069
You have to observe closely, observe...

770
01:00:23.153 --> 01:00:26.739
If we'd given them Woo-sung,
he'd be in a foreign...

771
01:00:26.822 --> 01:00:27.365
Hey!

772
01:00:27.448 --> 01:00:28.491
Shut it! Shut it!

773
01:00:28.574 --> 01:00:30.326
Shut the window!

774
01:00:36.207 --> 01:00:38.209
Hurry!

775
01:01:05.236 --> 01:01:06.905
We'll catch a cold.

776
01:01:06.988 --> 01:01:09.866
Grab clothes in the
back to change into.

777
01:01:18.374 --> 01:01:20.335
So, your driver's license...

778
01:01:20.460 --> 01:01:21.669
Huh?

779
01:01:21.752 --> 01:01:23.629
It says Ha Jin-young.

780
01:01:24.255 --> 01:01:27.425
Sang-hyun was my
nickname in the military.

781
01:01:27.717 --> 01:01:31.179
You never went to the military!

782
01:01:31.262 --> 01:01:32.973
Don't be a smart ass.

783
01:01:33.181 --> 01:01:38.228
What about you? "Oh, I get seasick..."

784
01:01:38.353 --> 01:01:39.604
Wasn't that totally realistic?

785
01:01:39.729 --> 01:01:42.941
Realistic? That was totally stupid.

786
01:01:43.108 --> 01:01:44.359
Hae-jin was way better.

787
01:01:44.442 --> 01:01:46.444
Woo-hoo!

788
01:01:47.528 --> 01:01:49.906
Actually the name Sang-hyun

789
01:01:49.990 --> 01:01:53.784
is what I wanted to
name my son if I had one.

790
01:01:54.244 --> 01:01:55.536
Really?

791
01:01:56.246 --> 01:01:57.663
Really.

792
01:02:00.416 --> 01:02:02.710
I won't laugh, then.

793
01:02:08.884 --> 01:02:10.635
It's So-young...

794
01:02:12.762 --> 01:02:15.556
My real name. Moon So-young.

795
01:02:15.681 --> 01:02:16.850
Who's Sun-ah?

796
01:02:16.933 --> 01:02:20.353
This obnoxious lady
who lives next door.

797
01:02:21.855 --> 01:02:24.900
This car is filled with liars.

798
01:02:58.183 --> 01:03:00.560
Since it's turned out this way,

799
01:03:01.727 --> 01:03:03.688
should we use it?

800
01:03:04.147 --> 01:03:05.648
The murder charge?

801
01:03:40.683 --> 01:03:42.102
Hello?

802
01:03:44.770 --> 01:03:46.481
Who is this?

803
01:03:48.691 --> 01:03:50.818
Hand over the baby.

804
01:03:51.694 --> 01:03:55.740
I paid your so-called mom before.

805
01:03:56.032 --> 01:03:57.825
5 million won.

806
01:03:59.870 --> 01:04:02.788
In return you were
supposed to abort it,

807
01:04:03.373 --> 01:04:05.750
but then you had to go have the baby...

808
01:04:18.763 --> 01:04:20.556
Ms. Moon So-young?

809
01:04:21.016 --> 01:04:22.767
We're from the police.

810
01:04:22.976 --> 01:04:25.020
Can we talk for a moment?

811
01:05:04.475 --> 01:05:05.685
You're back?

812
01:05:05.768 --> 01:05:07.103
You're back?

813
01:05:07.187 --> 01:05:08.438
Took you a while.

814
01:05:08.521 --> 01:05:11.024
We're drafting a
three-person work schedule.

815
01:05:11.191 --> 01:05:12.233
Work schedule?

816
01:05:12.525 --> 01:05:14.694
For feeding Woo-sung.

817
01:05:16.112 --> 01:05:18.114
Did you hear good news or something?

818
01:05:18.239 --> 01:05:18.990
Yeah.

819
01:05:19.615 --> 01:05:23.786
There's a buyer in Seoul
who will pay 30 million.

820
01:05:25.746 --> 01:05:28.583
Wow, bonanza...

821
01:05:29.918 --> 01:05:32.420
You're giving him a bath?

822
01:05:32.712 --> 01:05:36.049
He got poop smeared on his bum.

823
01:05:36.424 --> 01:05:39.052
Sang-hyun is so bad at this.

824
01:05:39.886 --> 01:05:45.225
How about 2-hour shifts
from 10 p.m. to 6 a.m.?

825
01:05:46.309 --> 01:05:48.979
Sang, Dong, So, Dong, Sang...

826
01:05:49.354 --> 01:05:52.773
This lets you sleep
for 6 hours straight!

827
01:05:52.899 --> 01:05:56.194
Not so much... can't we do this?

828
01:05:56.361 --> 01:05:58.696
- This is pretty unfair.
- Really?

829
01:05:58.779 --> 01:06:00.156
- I'll do it!
- What?

830
01:06:00.240 --> 01:06:01.699
Feed Woo-sung.

831
01:06:01.950 --> 01:06:04.494
- From 4 a.m. to 6 a.m.?
- Sure.

832
01:06:05.828 --> 01:06:09.124
Or how about 10 p.m. to midnight?

833
01:06:09.207 --> 01:06:11.459
Don't give him your shift!

834
01:06:14.587 --> 01:06:17.007
She agreed easily, right?

835
01:06:18.424 --> 01:06:20.010
She did.

836
01:06:21.636 --> 01:06:24.430
The reduced sentence
must've convinced her...

837
01:06:24.514 --> 01:06:25.765
No.

838
01:06:25.848 --> 01:06:27.642
I don't think it's that.

839
01:06:28.434 --> 01:06:30.103
Then what?

840
01:06:31.604 --> 01:06:33.439
I don't know either.

841
01:06:34.149 --> 01:06:37.152
I'm not sure, but...

842
01:06:38.444 --> 01:06:41.031
it wasn't the reduced sentence.

843
01:06:53.293 --> 01:06:54.794
How is he?

844
01:06:54.920 --> 01:06:56.337
Did he eat?

845
01:06:56.421 --> 01:06:58.506
No, he threw up again.

846
01:07:01.051 --> 01:07:04.595
Did you let it cool properly?
It's not too hot?

847
01:07:06.431 --> 01:07:08.099
It's fine.

848
01:07:08.224 --> 01:07:11.144
Was it because he got wet in the car?

849
01:07:11.519 --> 01:07:13.063
I'm sorry, Woo-sung.

850
01:07:13.146 --> 01:07:15.148
No, it's not because of you.

851
01:07:15.773 --> 01:07:18.401
Doesn't seem like an ordinary cold.

852
01:07:19.110 --> 01:07:21.779
Has this happened before?

853
01:07:24.240 --> 01:07:25.867
We should go to the hospital.

854
01:07:27.827 --> 01:07:29.537
We can't do that.

855
01:07:30.038 --> 01:07:31.957
We could get caught.

856
01:07:46.387 --> 01:07:49.599
It's not cerebromeningitis, is it?

857
01:07:50.058 --> 01:07:52.602
The fever came on yesterday...

858
01:07:54.270 --> 01:07:56.272
Will he get better?

859
01:07:57.232 --> 01:07:59.234
He won't die, will he?

860
01:08:02.195 --> 01:08:04.072
Is he your brother?

861
01:08:06.074 --> 01:08:07.367
Yes.

862
01:08:07.868 --> 01:08:10.078
It's okay. He won't die.

863
01:08:12.080 --> 01:08:13.664
It looks like a cold,

864
01:08:13.915 --> 01:08:17.085
but watch him to be sure it
doesn't turn into pneumonia.

865
01:08:17.167 --> 01:08:22.257
I'll prescribe a fever reducer,
but if it doesn't go down,

866
01:08:22.340 --> 01:08:24.217
come back tomorrow.

867
01:08:25.635 --> 01:08:28.053
What a relief, Woo-sung.

868
01:08:29.847 --> 01:08:37.230
♪ If affection is even ♪
♪ sadder than love... ♪

869
01:08:37.312 --> 01:08:39.357
Will the baby be okay?

870
01:08:41.566 --> 01:08:43.611
They're all overreacting.

871
01:08:44.069 --> 01:08:46.865
It's just a cold.

872
01:08:47.072 --> 01:08:49.074
Yes, but still...

873
01:08:50.160 --> 01:08:53.246
If he doesn't get better
soon, it's a real problem.

874
01:08:55.540 --> 01:08:57.457
Because they can't sell him?

875
01:09:02.380 --> 01:09:06.634
If they can't sell him, we
can't arrest them in the act.

876
01:09:07.842 --> 01:09:10.138
We're the Female Youth Division,

877
01:09:10.220 --> 01:09:14.642
we should throw our net further
up the river than Criminal Affairs.

878
01:09:16.895 --> 01:09:18.728
Up the river?

879
01:09:19.147 --> 01:09:22.317
Shouldn't we have saved her
before she threw away her child?

880
01:09:22.400 --> 01:09:24.734
That's for Welfare Services.

881
01:09:24.819 --> 01:09:28.531
Welfare before she abandons
him, the police after.

882
01:09:29.407 --> 01:09:31.326
Really...

883
01:09:33.328 --> 01:09:36.414
Why are you so cold towards that woman?

884
01:09:42.752 --> 01:09:44.672
She's irresponsible.

885
01:09:46.756 --> 01:09:49.594
Have the baby, then
abandon him on a whim...

886
01:09:50.803 --> 01:09:55.100
Still, to judge her so quickly...

887
01:09:57.518 --> 01:10:01.106
Can you understand a woman
who throws away her baby?

888
01:10:03.691 --> 01:10:05.443
I can't.

889
01:10:14.327 --> 01:10:15.954
You can't do that here.

890
01:10:16.037 --> 01:10:17.538
This isn't a playground.

891
01:10:17.622 --> 01:10:19.540
You're right.

892
01:10:20.500 --> 01:10:22.835
- You're his father?
- Yes.

893
01:10:24.295 --> 01:10:25.964
There are other patients here.

894
01:10:26.047 --> 01:10:27.465
- Please control him.
- I will.

895
01:10:27.548 --> 01:10:29.550
Are you Woo-sung's father?

896
01:10:29.717 --> 01:10:32.929
Yes... sure...

897
01:10:33.263 --> 01:10:35.932
What's his national ID number?

898
01:10:37.308 --> 01:10:40.561
Actually, he's still
just a month old, so...

899
01:10:41.271 --> 01:10:42.438
One month?

900
01:10:42.522 --> 01:10:44.815
Yes, no one can believe it.

901
01:10:46.026 --> 01:10:47.986
Is it the formula?

902
01:10:48.069 --> 01:10:49.737
The American brand. What's it called?

903
01:10:49.820 --> 01:10:51.322
Similac.

904
01:10:51.822 --> 01:10:56.619
The boy's grandma gave
us so much of that Similac...

905
01:10:56.702 --> 01:10:58.038
Right,

906
01:10:58.121 --> 01:11:01.082
she was so happy to
have her first grandson.

907
01:11:01.499 --> 01:11:04.044
Then can you come with me for a moment?

908
01:11:04.377 --> 01:11:05.795
Sure.

909
01:11:08.464 --> 01:11:11.885
That punk, playing soccer all day long.

910
01:11:12.010 --> 01:11:16.306
That's why the director
blows his whistle so much.

911
01:11:17.974 --> 01:11:19.725
Going on and on...

912
01:11:24.272 --> 01:11:26.357
Thank you for doing this.

913
01:11:27.108 --> 01:11:31.196
All kids get fevers, it's normal.

914
01:11:32.530 --> 01:11:35.491
If I were alone, I'd
have been helpless.

915
01:11:35.951 --> 01:11:39.662
No need to do it all yourself.

916
01:11:44.125 --> 01:11:48.671
And the father...

917
01:11:49.505 --> 01:11:52.050
He was against it from the start.

918
01:11:53.885 --> 01:11:56.637
I see. That's too bad...

919
01:12:25.833 --> 01:12:29.337
It seems this woman
ran away with a baby.

920
01:12:30.046 --> 01:12:31.965
Find her and bring it back.

921
01:12:33.174 --> 01:12:34.842
Bring her back?

922
01:12:35.176 --> 01:12:36.844
The baby.

923
01:12:38.513 --> 01:12:40.806
What will you do with it?

924
01:12:44.727 --> 01:12:46.354
Raise it.

925
01:12:46.729 --> 01:12:48.314
Myself.

926
01:12:48.648 --> 01:12:51.067
Since it's my husband's.

927
01:13:00.618 --> 01:13:02.203
Fully automated?

928
01:13:02.828 --> 01:13:04.539
Are they kidding?

929
01:13:05.248 --> 01:13:07.292
What do I do with this?

930
01:13:15.258 --> 01:13:17.010
Dammit.

931
01:13:19.845 --> 01:13:21.389
Hi, Tae-ho.

932
01:13:21.597 --> 01:13:25.185
I'm sorry, I'll get you the money soon.

933
01:13:29.314 --> 01:13:30.731
What?

934
01:13:30.899 --> 01:13:33.193
The baby? Who?

935
01:13:37.405 --> 01:13:39.407
Woo-sung's father?

936
01:13:40.366 --> 01:13:42.077
For how much?

937
01:13:43.744 --> 01:13:45.288
40 million?

938
01:13:50.335 --> 01:13:52.420
He's passed out cold.

939
01:13:54.089 --> 01:13:56.007
Must've been tired.

940
01:13:56.216 --> 01:13:59.177
All day he was
worrying it was his fault.

941
01:14:02.513 --> 01:14:04.640
He's like Si-woo, this kid.

942
01:14:06.559 --> 01:14:09.645
The type that gets left behind.

943
01:14:11.857 --> 01:14:14.901
Did you ever want to be adopted?

944
01:14:17.403 --> 01:14:19.739
I liked it there.

945
01:14:20.156 --> 01:14:22.617
I told them I didn't
want to be adopted.

946
01:14:24.160 --> 01:14:26.621
You thought your mom would come back?

947
01:14:29.958 --> 01:14:32.168
So Sang-hyun's been talking.

948
01:14:33.128 --> 01:14:35.922
Yeah, about the letter.

949
01:14:39.300 --> 01:14:42.553
I never thought of myself as abandoned.

950
01:14:49.560 --> 01:14:51.187
He's asleep.

951
01:14:54.190 --> 01:14:55.733
Will you wash it?

952
01:14:55.816 --> 01:14:57.944
You do it, please.

953
01:15:00.488 --> 01:15:02.657
Put his chin into your shoulder.

954
01:15:03.033 --> 01:15:04.825
I know how.

955
01:15:05.576 --> 01:15:06.619
No, higher.

956
01:15:06.702 --> 01:15:08.079
I know!

957
01:15:08.872 --> 01:15:09.830
That's too weak.

958
01:15:09.915 --> 01:15:11.207
Be quiet...

959
01:15:16.087 --> 01:15:18.673
You're not caring for him on purpose?

960
01:15:18.924 --> 01:15:20.258
What?

961
01:15:23.136 --> 01:15:25.555
In case you won't be
able to let go later.

962
01:15:31.227 --> 01:15:32.854
Why are you laughing?

963
01:15:33.813 --> 01:15:37.358
Women will eat you
alive if you're so nice.

964
01:15:40.361 --> 01:15:42.906
That's exactly what Sang-hyun said.

965
01:15:59.881 --> 01:16:01.174
Where are you going?

966
01:16:01.257 --> 01:16:02.592
The convenience store.

967
01:16:02.675 --> 01:16:04.052
Want me to go?

968
01:16:04.135 --> 01:16:08.264
There are things a woman
can't ask a man to buy.

969
01:16:08.764 --> 01:16:11.935
It might rain. Take an umbrella.

970
01:16:12.978 --> 01:16:15.313
Come and get me if it rains.

971
01:16:17.065 --> 01:16:18.859
With an umbrella.

972
01:16:22.695 --> 01:16:24.322
No.

973
01:16:24.990 --> 01:16:26.950
I'll be back!

974
01:16:34.790 --> 01:16:37.878
Where'd you meet the
woman you call Mom?

975
01:16:38.711 --> 01:16:41.714
I had run away, and was
sleeping at Songdo Beach.

976
01:16:41.923 --> 01:16:44.509
She asked if I was hungry.

977
01:16:45.801 --> 01:16:48.846
Did she force you into prostitution?

978
01:16:53.268 --> 01:16:55.436
Are you taking pity on me?

979
01:16:57.438 --> 01:16:58.439
No, it's not that.

980
01:16:58.523 --> 01:17:01.067
I did it even before meeting Mom.

981
01:17:02.193 --> 01:17:05.113
Then why kill that guy?

982
01:17:06.781 --> 01:17:08.324
Well...

983
01:17:09.075 --> 01:17:10.743
I got upset.

984
01:17:11.452 --> 01:17:13.038
Upset?

985
01:17:13.413 --> 01:17:16.917
He told me to lick him
before he took a shower.

986
01:17:18.209 --> 01:17:21.379
Did he do anything to
make it self-defense?

987
01:17:21.462 --> 01:17:24.840
I can give you a list of my
customers if you want.

988
01:17:27.218 --> 01:17:29.971
No need. What I want to know is...

989
01:17:30.055 --> 01:17:32.432
Is this an investigation, or a lecture?

990
01:17:32.765 --> 01:17:35.518
I'll sell the baby as you
told me to, don't worry.

991
01:17:36.978 --> 01:17:40.440
We want to help. Both of us.

992
01:17:44.485 --> 01:17:46.654
Have you ever abandoned a baby?

993
01:17:46.863 --> 01:17:48.781
Or killed someone?

994
01:17:49.240 --> 01:17:53.119
Fine, then tell us. Because
I can't understand.

995
01:17:55.663 --> 01:17:57.457
Why'd you abandon him?

996
01:17:57.540 --> 01:17:59.542
Outside the box, even.

997
01:18:04.547 --> 01:18:06.299
You saw it?

998
01:18:10.136 --> 01:18:12.472
He'd have died if you left him.

999
01:18:15.558 --> 01:18:18.186
I never intended to see him again.

1000
01:18:19.020 --> 01:18:21.606
Then why have him
if you can't raise him?

1001
01:18:21.689 --> 01:18:23.149
I should've aborted him?

1002
01:18:23.233 --> 01:18:26.444
Thinking of him, might that be better?

1003
01:18:28.488 --> 01:18:31.867
Rather than throw him away,
killing him before he's born

1004
01:18:32.533 --> 01:18:34.494
is less of a sin?

1005
01:18:43.294 --> 01:18:44.670
If nobody wants him,

1006
01:18:44.754 --> 01:18:47.673
giving birth will just
make him miserable.

1007
01:18:47.757 --> 01:18:50.801
Say that in front of Woo-sung,
that I should've killed him first!

1008
01:18:50.886 --> 01:18:53.138
You threw him away!

1009
01:19:31.092 --> 01:19:32.468
Hi.

1010
01:19:35.471 --> 01:19:37.682
Hey, listen.

1011
01:19:38.433 --> 01:19:42.395
Can you bring me some
clothes? My button fell off.

1012
01:19:43.897 --> 01:19:47.067
We're in Uljin.

1013
01:19:52.363 --> 01:19:54.407
Yeah, right?

1014
01:19:59.079 --> 01:20:01.039
Never mind, it's okay.

1015
01:20:04.709 --> 01:20:08.254
Check this out. Listen to this song.

1016
01:20:18.306 --> 01:20:19.807
Hello?

1017
01:20:20.266 --> 01:20:24.520
Did you hear it? Remember,
that movie we saw?

1018
01:20:25.313 --> 01:20:27.440
It was in that.

1019
01:20:31.777 --> 01:20:33.238
Right...

1020
01:20:35.240 --> 01:20:39.702
Though it doesn't
make sense in reality.

1021
01:20:45.583 --> 01:20:47.543
Rice? What rice?

1022
01:20:47.668 --> 01:20:49.504
Ah, like at a wedding?

1023
01:20:58.846 --> 01:21:01.224
No, things are fine.

1024
01:21:05.436 --> 01:21:06.980
Sorry.

1025
01:21:15.196 --> 01:21:16.781
Just because.

1026
01:21:28.709 --> 01:21:30.545
Stick the needle in here.

1027
01:21:31.212 --> 01:21:34.215
Under the button. Look.

1028
01:21:35.216 --> 01:21:40.180
If you wrap it around a
few times, it won't fall off.

1029
01:21:40.388 --> 01:21:42.098
Wow, Dong-soo, how'd you do that?

1030
01:21:42.182 --> 01:21:43.892
- Hae-jin, you try it.
- I wanna try!

1031
01:21:44.184 --> 01:21:45.476
Come on, try it.

1032
01:21:45.560 --> 01:21:47.478
No, I wanna do this.

1033
01:21:52.317 --> 01:21:55.320
So who are we meeting tomorrow?

1034
01:21:55.445 --> 01:21:57.948
They're rich, of course.

1035
01:21:58.698 --> 01:22:01.117
Since they're offering 40 million.

1036
01:22:01.201 --> 01:22:02.577
30 million.

1037
01:22:02.660 --> 01:22:05.621
Right, 30 million.

1038
01:22:06.539 --> 01:22:09.209
Why? Who would you prefer?

1039
01:22:10.210 --> 01:22:12.963
Someone pretty like So-young.

1040
01:22:13.463 --> 01:22:15.131
Hey, Dong-soo.

1041
01:22:15.590 --> 01:22:17.383
Learn from him.

1042
01:22:17.592 --> 01:22:20.845
A man needs to slip in
praise casually like that.

1043
01:22:20.929 --> 01:22:23.681
Thank you for your instruction, Master.

1044
01:22:23.764 --> 01:22:26.559
What? I didn't hear you.

1045
01:22:27.435 --> 01:22:31.397
They say the eldest son resembles
the mom, and the daughter the dad.

1046
01:22:31.481 --> 01:22:33.733
That's why my daughter is doomed.

1047
01:22:34.150 --> 01:22:36.361
It's okay, you don't live with her.

1048
01:22:36.777 --> 01:22:38.654
That's just superstition.

1049
01:22:38.905 --> 01:22:42.117
So you're an eldest daughter?

1050
01:22:42.200 --> 01:22:43.076
Shut up.

1051
01:22:43.159 --> 01:22:45.036
When I look at old photos of my mom,

1052
01:22:45.120 --> 01:22:47.622
sometimes I think it's me.

1053
01:22:50.416 --> 01:22:53.128
That button was about to fall off.

1054
01:22:59.550 --> 01:23:02.053
- Where are you going?
- To wash up.

1055
01:23:07.767 --> 01:23:12.813
That kid doesn't know
his parents' faces, either.

1056
01:23:14.107 --> 01:23:19.487
Sometimes, you know,
it's better that way.

1057
01:23:26.161 --> 01:23:30.874
For Woo-sung too, it'll be better
if he can't remember my face.

1058
01:23:33.418 --> 01:23:35.378
Why do you say that?

1059
01:23:38.423 --> 01:23:40.466
Because I'm a murderer.

1060
01:23:42.052 --> 01:23:43.719
Murder?

1061
01:23:44.429 --> 01:23:45.721
Yeah.

1062
01:23:48.099 --> 01:23:49.767
Who'd you kill?

1063
01:23:52.145 --> 01:23:54.147
Woo-sung's father.

1064
01:23:58.568 --> 01:24:00.070
Why?

1065
01:24:07.953 --> 01:24:10.914
He said Woo-sung should
never have been born,

1066
01:24:12.290 --> 01:24:14.876
tried to take him from me.

1067
01:24:18.421 --> 01:24:19.839
What?

1068
01:24:22.508 --> 01:24:25.971
His wife is probably
searching for me now.

1069
01:24:30.516 --> 01:24:35.063
So if you'll sell him properly,
you can leave me behind.

1070
01:24:44.865 --> 01:24:47.117
I just came out of the hotel.

1071
01:24:47.909 --> 01:24:50.786
And... hold on a sec.

1072
01:24:54.082 --> 01:24:56.251
Let me ask you something.

1073
01:24:56.417 --> 01:24:58.044
Sang-hyun.

1074
01:25:01.089 --> 01:25:02.966
What are you doing here?

1075
01:25:03.091 --> 01:25:07.595
After what So-young told us, I
thought I'd check just in case.

1076
01:25:08.554 --> 01:25:09.722
Look.

1077
01:25:09.805 --> 01:25:11.641
What is that?

1078
01:25:12.808 --> 01:25:16.146
This is a GPS or something.
Where'd you find it?

1079
01:25:16.229 --> 01:25:17.898
In here.

1080
01:25:20.608 --> 01:25:22.110
The cops?

1081
01:25:22.568 --> 01:25:25.947
The cops wouldn't use
an antique like this.

1082
01:25:26.822 --> 01:25:30.160
Then someone's been following us.

1083
01:25:30.326 --> 01:25:34.580
Don't you think?
From the father's side.

1084
01:25:39.002 --> 01:25:40.045
Don't do it.

1085
01:25:40.128 --> 01:25:41.046
What?

1086
01:25:41.796 --> 01:25:44.840
You were planning to
leave without So-young.

1087
01:25:45.466 --> 01:25:46.426
Well...

1088
01:25:49.888 --> 01:25:51.932
This time rather than money,

1089
01:25:52.307 --> 01:25:56.978
let's find a buyer
So-young is happy with.

1090
01:25:58.229 --> 01:26:02.192
I don't care only about
money, you know.

1091
01:26:02.984 --> 01:26:04.777
Good, then.

1092
01:26:06.071 --> 01:26:08.281
I'll take care of this, then.

1093
01:26:11.117 --> 01:26:12.618
What?

1094
01:26:13.912 --> 01:26:15.746
What are you doing?

1095
01:26:40.480 --> 01:26:42.482
I know everything.

1096
01:26:42.607 --> 01:26:45.651
Woo-sung's dad is dead.

1097
01:26:46.361 --> 01:26:49.572
So what? As long as you get paid.

1098
01:26:52.117 --> 01:26:55.495
But who wants to buy him?

1099
01:26:58.748 --> 01:27:00.625
The dead man's wife.

1100
01:27:01.001 --> 01:27:03.086
What'll she do with him?

1101
01:27:04.129 --> 01:27:05.713
She says she'll raise him.

1102
01:27:05.796 --> 01:27:08.674
Raise him? Don't talk nonsense.

1103
01:27:08.799 --> 01:27:10.843
She'll sell him, right?

1104
01:27:11.011 --> 01:27:13.096
Ship him abroad?

1105
01:27:13.263 --> 01:27:14.722
I'm not selling.

1106
01:27:15.306 --> 01:27:17.558
Come out here, now!

1107
01:27:17.642 --> 01:27:19.352
Hey, hey.

1108
01:27:20.770 --> 01:27:22.563
Who the hell are you?

1109
01:27:23.148 --> 01:27:27.110
You're on the father's side?

1110
01:27:27.193 --> 01:27:29.404
Shut up and give me the
baby. Come out here!

1111
01:27:29.487 --> 01:27:30.864
Come out!

1112
01:27:31.948 --> 01:27:33.449
Hey!

1113
01:27:41.249 --> 01:27:43.459
Careful!

1114
01:27:45.836 --> 01:27:48.423
Hey, did you kill him?

1115
01:27:49.590 --> 01:27:52.385
He's the son of someone I know!

1116
01:27:52.718 --> 01:27:54.679
He's fine, just passed out.

1117
01:27:54.930 --> 01:27:56.014
Dammit.

1118
01:27:59.976 --> 01:28:01.769
Help me out.

1119
01:28:20.038 --> 01:28:21.915
Where are they going now?

1120
01:28:21.998 --> 01:28:24.876
They're driving south on this road,

1121
01:28:25.001 --> 01:28:27.045
but I think we can catch up in 5km.

1122
01:28:27.128 --> 01:28:28.629
- Speed up, then.
- Okay.

1123
01:28:28.713 --> 01:28:30.506
We were careless.

1124
01:28:38.139 --> 01:28:39.975
It's the KTX! KTX!

1125
01:29:18.263 --> 01:29:20.181
I had a dream.

1126
01:29:21.432 --> 01:29:27.397
Years ago I took this train with
my daughter, wife and mother

1127
01:29:27.480 --> 01:29:29.565
and went to Wolmido.

1128
01:29:30.984 --> 01:29:33.736
- Back then...
- A good dream, then.

1129
01:29:34.029 --> 01:29:36.281
No, not really.

1130
01:29:42.871 --> 01:29:46.249
Why do you think she told us?

1131
01:29:46.958 --> 01:29:49.252
- Their destination?
- Yes.

1132
01:29:52.630 --> 01:29:55.425
She wants us to follow?

1133
01:29:55.758 --> 01:29:59.679
So that Woo-sung
doesn't get taken away?

1134
01:30:02.515 --> 01:30:05.018
That may be what she's thinking.

1135
01:30:19.532 --> 01:30:21.242
Will it be okay?

1136
01:30:21.492 --> 01:30:23.286
It's my treat.

1137
01:30:24.245 --> 01:30:26.081
Not this.

1138
01:30:29.084 --> 01:30:31.502
I may just go myself.

1139
01:30:33.754 --> 01:30:38.093
That's okay, as long as they
don't pay in installments.

1140
01:30:40.220 --> 01:30:42.305
- So-young.
- Yeah?

1141
01:30:43.806 --> 01:30:47.936
When you put Woo-sung in the box...

1142
01:30:49.770 --> 01:30:54.775
I mean, did you really
think of coming back?

1143
01:31:01.657 --> 01:31:03.493
No?

1144
01:31:05.245 --> 01:31:06.913
I'm not sure.

1145
01:31:10.291 --> 01:31:16.381
But if I'd met you a bit earlier,

1146
01:31:19.217 --> 01:31:22.178
maybe I wouldn't have had to.

1147
01:31:25.681 --> 01:31:28.059
It's not too late.

1148
01:31:28.894 --> 01:31:31.104
What did you say?

1149
01:31:32.563 --> 01:31:34.482
What? Never mind.

1150
01:31:38.945 --> 01:31:42.365
You're keeping
So-young all to yourself!

1151
01:31:43.283 --> 01:31:45.785
All right, take the baton.

1152
01:31:51.875 --> 01:31:54.335
What kind of guy do you like?

1153
01:31:54.710 --> 01:31:56.129
Huh?

1154
01:31:58.839 --> 01:32:00.508
I don't know.

1155
01:32:01.217 --> 01:32:04.137
A guy like you who
looks good in overalls.

1156
01:32:07.557 --> 01:32:10.894
Hae-jin is a great name.

1157
01:32:11.895 --> 01:32:15.982
I like your name. It means
going out to the sea.

1158
01:32:17.275 --> 01:32:21.529
When you grow up, you'll
probably work abroad.

1159
01:32:22.197 --> 01:32:24.365
In the Premier League?

1160
01:32:25.951 --> 01:32:27.452
Sure.

1161
01:32:29.704 --> 01:32:33.291
- Who named Woo-sung?
- Me.

1162
01:32:33.708 --> 01:32:35.460
Lucky him.

1163
01:32:35.668 --> 01:32:38.546
What does it mean?

1164
01:32:43.676 --> 01:32:47.763
"Woo" means wings, and
"sung" means the stars.

1165
01:32:48.181 --> 01:32:50.892
I hope he goes far, far away.

1166
01:32:51.184 --> 01:32:56.772
If you cross the sea,
Woo-sung will go to the stars.

1167
01:32:57.482 --> 01:32:59.442
<i>Like an astronaut?</i>

1168
01:32:59.734 --> 01:33:01.652
<i>Or a pilot?</i>

1169
01:33:02.820 --> 01:33:05.115
<i>We're like brothers.</i>

1170
01:33:31.057 --> 01:33:32.392
Hello?

1171
01:33:32.475 --> 01:33:35.854
I'm wondering if we can
meet two hours earlier?

1172
01:33:36.062 --> 01:33:37.522
See you at 12.

1173
01:33:37.605 --> 01:33:40.066
Yes, thank you.

1174
01:33:48.074 --> 01:33:50.576
Today is about Woo-sung.

1175
01:33:51.077 --> 01:33:52.453
Got it?

1176
01:33:52.537 --> 01:33:55.081
- Can't I be adopted too?
- No.

1177
01:33:55.165 --> 01:33:56.541
No way.

1178
01:34:09.012 --> 01:34:13.683
Thank you so much for
agreeing to our request.

1179
01:34:14.475 --> 01:34:17.103
As I told you already,

1180
01:34:19.022 --> 01:34:22.692
our baby was stillborn.

1181
01:34:23.151 --> 01:34:26.154
Since it could well happen again...

1182
01:34:26.821 --> 01:34:29.365
It must've been hard on you.

1183
01:34:29.950 --> 01:34:35.538
It was a girl, a cute
baby just like him.

1184
01:34:36.539 --> 01:34:40.919
Have a seat. Would you
like coffee? Ice coffee?

1185
01:34:41.627 --> 01:34:43.088
Yes.

1186
01:34:44.380 --> 01:34:48.468
Could I hold him?

1187
01:34:48.551 --> 01:34:50.303
Yes, sure.

1188
01:34:55.016 --> 01:34:56.184
Woo-sung.

1189
01:35:00.981 --> 01:35:03.358
It's okay, don't be scared.

1190
01:35:03.441 --> 01:35:05.568
Is he hungry? The bottle...

1191
01:35:05.651 --> 01:35:07.362
Were you hungry?

1192
01:35:07.863 --> 01:35:13.368
If you don't mind, could
I try breast feeding him?

1193
01:35:13.451 --> 01:35:15.871
It's okay?

1194
01:35:16.287 --> 01:35:20.250
- Then, over here.
- Thank you.

1195
01:35:23.628 --> 01:35:25.296
Woo-sung.

1196
01:35:26.047 --> 01:35:27.548
It's okay...

1197
01:35:28.008 --> 01:35:29.592
It's okay...

1198
01:35:31.469 --> 01:35:33.054
Oh my.

1199
01:35:36.266 --> 01:35:38.726
Look, he's eating.

1200
01:35:40.937 --> 01:35:42.688
Is that good?

1201
01:35:43.314 --> 01:35:45.441
Does it taste good?

1202
01:35:51.156 --> 01:35:56.452
I didn't mention this in my email,
but can I propose one condition?

1203
01:35:57.620 --> 01:35:59.789
Thinking of the future,

1204
01:36:00.290 --> 01:36:03.751
we want to raise
Woo-sung as our real child.

1205
01:36:04.252 --> 01:36:07.881
So we'd like for this to be

1206
01:36:08.589 --> 01:36:12.343
the last meeting between
him and his birth mother.

1207
01:36:13.136 --> 01:36:18.558
I know it will be hard, but
think it over for today.

1208
01:36:21.602 --> 01:36:22.979
Wow!

1209
01:36:31.321 --> 01:36:33.656
So-young, sit here!

1210
01:36:45.626 --> 01:36:48.171
That came out well.

1211
01:36:55.761 --> 01:36:58.056
Wow, a monorail!

1212
01:36:58.681 --> 01:37:00.016
Hi!

1213
01:37:00.976 --> 01:37:02.518
Hi!

1214
01:37:09.025 --> 01:37:10.610
Let's take photos!

1215
01:37:10.693 --> 01:37:12.195
Photos!

1216
01:37:12.778 --> 01:37:14.697
Let's go in!

1217
01:37:15.907 --> 01:37:17.617
How much is it?

1218
01:37:19.494 --> 01:37:21.287
4,000 won?

1219
01:37:28.086 --> 01:37:30.046
Not yet, we're not done.

1220
01:37:30.130 --> 01:37:30.838
Just a minute.

1221
01:37:30.922 --> 01:37:33.258
I want the monkey doll!

1222
01:37:33.758 --> 01:37:36.136
Oh no, I better not miss this.

1223
01:37:39.597 --> 01:37:40.556
Hold on.

1224
01:37:40.640 --> 01:37:41.682
Do it!

1225
01:37:46.562 --> 01:37:47.939
Hae-jin.

1226
01:37:48.023 --> 01:37:49.732
There's a soccer field. Look.

1227
01:37:49.815 --> 01:37:51.442
- Yeah.
- Huh?

1228
01:37:51.567 --> 01:37:53.319
It's a soccer field!

1229
01:37:54.737 --> 01:37:58.783
I don't like heights, I'm scared.

1230
01:37:59.159 --> 01:38:02.745
Hey, you said you wanted to ride this.

1231
01:38:03.329 --> 01:38:05.665
Back then... I was just improvising...

1232
01:38:06.332 --> 01:38:08.251
What's wrong?

1233
01:38:08.334 --> 01:38:10.295
You're not going to throw up?

1234
01:38:10.378 --> 01:38:12.755
You've gone pale. Are you okay?

1235
01:38:12.923 --> 01:38:15.716
- Don't throw up.
- Yeah.

1236
01:38:16.092 --> 01:38:18.803
- Don't throw up here.
- Yeah.

1237
01:38:18.929 --> 01:38:22.891
Look at you, I wanted to treat you.

1238
01:38:23.099 --> 01:38:24.935
Bring me there instead.

1239
01:38:25.018 --> 01:38:25.726
Where?

1240
01:38:25.810 --> 01:38:26.811
The car wash.

1241
01:38:26.895 --> 01:38:28.063
What?

1242
01:38:28.146 --> 01:38:29.022
The car wash.

1243
01:38:29.105 --> 01:38:30.941
- The car wash?
- Yeah.

1244
01:38:31.274 --> 01:38:34.569
- You like getting soaked?
- Yeah.

1245
01:38:36.071 --> 01:38:40.200
Okay, if things go well
tomorrow, let's go again.

1246
01:38:40.783 --> 01:38:42.994
Tell me when we reach the ground.

1247
01:38:43.078 --> 01:38:44.454
Okay.

1248
01:38:45.246 --> 01:38:47.332
- Don't throw up.
- Yeah.

1249
01:38:47.457 --> 01:38:49.292
You punk.

1250
01:39:05.892 --> 01:39:08.103
Should we look a bit longer?

1251
01:39:12.899 --> 01:39:16.611
Or we could not put
him up for adoption.

1252
01:39:20.531 --> 01:39:21.992
Still...

1253
01:39:24.327 --> 01:39:26.121
We could even

1254
01:39:26.787 --> 01:39:28.915
just raise him ourselves.

1255
01:39:32.460 --> 01:39:33.962
We?

1256
01:39:35.546 --> 01:39:37.048
The four of us.

1257
01:39:38.674 --> 01:39:42.262
Or with Hae-jin. Five would be nice.

1258
01:39:45.140 --> 01:39:49.227
That's a strange family. Who's the dad?

1259
01:39:55.108 --> 01:39:57.402
I'll be Woo-sung's dad.

1260
01:40:01.990 --> 01:40:04.951
That's what men say when they propose.

1261
01:40:06.953 --> 01:40:08.579
Really?

1262
01:40:19.590 --> 01:40:22.928
I wish we could start
over again like that.

1263
01:40:36.858 --> 01:40:38.860
But it can't happen.

1264
01:40:40.987 --> 01:40:43.448
I'll be arrested soon.

1265
01:40:49.996 --> 01:40:56.002
"A Busan-based prostitute murdered
a man, and while on the run,

1266
01:40:56.336 --> 01:40:59.714
left her child in a baby box."

1267
01:41:12.268 --> 01:41:14.437
Is this how you'll appear?

1268
01:41:17.941 --> 01:41:20.526
These days they don't blur the faces.

1269
01:41:22.988 --> 01:41:24.530
They don't?

1270
01:41:31.162 --> 01:41:33.581
This thing's shaking, right?

1271
01:41:35.583 --> 01:41:39.004
It's okay. It's because
we're at the top.

1272
01:41:42.132 --> 01:41:44.968
It's even scarier, not
being able to see.

1273
01:41:46.219 --> 01:41:47.762
It's strange.

1274
01:42:03.111 --> 01:42:06.614
Seeing you makes my
heart feel a bit lighter.

1275
01:42:08.533 --> 01:42:10.201
In what way?

1276
01:42:11.077 --> 01:42:12.996
My mom too

1277
01:42:14.956 --> 01:42:18.793
may have had some unavoidable
reason to abandon me.

1278
01:42:28.887 --> 01:42:30.555
Even so,

1279
01:42:32.933 --> 01:42:35.643
you don't need to forgive her.

1280
01:42:37.437 --> 01:42:40.857
She's still an awful mother.

1281
01:42:49.407 --> 01:42:50.867
Then,

1282
01:42:53.244 --> 01:42:55.956
instead I'll forgive you.

1283
01:43:09.594 --> 01:43:12.555
Woo-sung will never forgive me.

1284
01:43:17.810 --> 01:43:19.645
You abandoned him

1285
01:43:21.106 --> 01:43:24.650
so he wouldn't grow up
as a murderer's son.

1286
01:43:31.574 --> 01:43:33.409
Still,

1287
01:43:36.329 --> 01:43:38.623
I threw him away.

1288
01:43:59.394 --> 01:44:03.106
I guess I'm the one who
wanted to sell him the most.

1289
01:44:07.110 --> 01:44:09.695
We're more like brokers than they are.

1290
01:44:30.050 --> 01:44:34.720
It was the same with you,
when you were young.

1291
01:44:34.971 --> 01:44:37.140
You almost threw up,

1292
01:44:37.223 --> 01:44:40.226
but you didn't, I held you...

1293
01:44:40.894 --> 01:44:44.940
I don't remember. I
was three years old.

1294
01:44:46.732 --> 01:44:49.069
Was it that long ago?

1295
01:44:51.071 --> 01:44:56.326
Wow, you're already solving
such difficult problems?

1296
01:45:00.997 --> 01:45:03.541
What? Who is it?

1297
01:45:04.125 --> 01:45:05.501
Mom.

1298
01:45:05.585 --> 01:45:07.045
Answer it.

1299
01:45:08.546 --> 01:45:09.714
Is it a message?

1300
01:45:09.797 --> 01:45:11.257
Answer her.

1301
01:45:11.591 --> 01:45:13.759
Should we send her a selfie?

1302
01:45:13.843 --> 01:45:14.635
No.

1303
01:45:14.719 --> 01:45:17.513
Here's your order. Enjoy.

1304
01:45:19.140 --> 01:45:22.268
Eat some. It looks good.

1305
01:45:24.062 --> 01:45:28.524
Tomorrow I'm getting
paid a lot of money.

1306
01:45:29.442 --> 01:45:35.365
Then maybe the three of
us, like before, in Busan...

1307
01:45:36.449 --> 01:45:39.327
Or I can come to Seoul.

1308
01:45:40.703 --> 01:45:45.291
We don't need money, just stop calling.

1309
01:45:46.960 --> 01:45:49.462
That's what Mom said.

1310
01:45:50.755 --> 01:45:53.341
Ah, Mom...

1311
01:45:56.802 --> 01:46:00.848
But really, she said not
to come to the house.

1312
01:46:04.019 --> 01:46:07.981
Last time I drank too much...

1313
01:46:08.064 --> 01:46:11.442
Look! This straw,

1314
01:46:11.985 --> 01:46:14.195
it's shaped like a heart.

1315
01:46:16.697 --> 01:46:18.241
Dad,

1316
01:46:19.450 --> 01:46:21.995
there's a new baby coming.

1317
01:46:24.622 --> 01:46:26.207
Mom's?

1318
01:46:27.042 --> 01:46:29.920
Yeah. A boy.

1319
01:46:34.007 --> 01:46:36.176
Is that so?

1320
01:46:39.720 --> 01:46:43.308
Then please say congratulations to Mom.

1321
01:46:45.143 --> 01:46:46.937
Sorry.

1322
01:46:48.146 --> 01:46:50.023
No, no...

1323
01:46:52.525 --> 01:46:57.780
Still, in the future...
I'm still your dad...

1324
01:46:58.448 --> 01:46:59.908
Right?

1325
01:47:01.659 --> 01:47:03.328
Really?

1326
01:47:08.083 --> 01:47:09.625
Of course.

1327
01:47:12.628 --> 01:47:14.255
I'll be going.

1328
01:47:17.633 --> 01:47:19.469
I'll see you.

1329
01:48:04.722 --> 01:48:06.724
Steak, steak!

1330
01:48:10.061 --> 01:48:14.232
To wish us success for tomorrow.

1331
01:48:24.325 --> 01:48:26.661
Woo-sung, say "My brother Hae-jin"!

1332
01:48:26.744 --> 01:48:28.746
"Hae-jin, Hae-jin"!

1333
01:48:30.373 --> 01:48:32.208
He said "Hae-jin"!

1334
01:48:32.542 --> 01:48:34.419
Yeah, right.

1335
01:48:35.253 --> 01:48:37.380
Woo-sung, you did, right?

1336
01:48:37.463 --> 01:48:39.215
He definitely did.

1337
01:48:39.632 --> 01:48:43.261
Woo-sung, you can't ever forget us!

1338
01:48:43.678 --> 01:48:45.846
He'll forget us right away.

1339
01:48:46.181 --> 01:48:50.435
Hae-jin, you can remember
all of this for him.

1340
01:48:51.686 --> 01:48:55.523
This guy is such a dork sometimes.

1341
01:48:55.606 --> 01:48:57.525
I totally agree.

1342
01:48:59.319 --> 01:49:02.113
Woo-sung, today was so much fun.

1343
01:49:02.697 --> 01:49:05.616
So let's not forget!

1344
01:49:07.285 --> 01:49:11.039
So-young, you never talk to Woo-sung.

1345
01:49:13.041 --> 01:49:14.042
That's not true.

1346
01:49:14.625 --> 01:49:17.753
He's right, I've never seen it.

1347
01:49:20.465 --> 01:49:23.218
It's the end, so say something.

1348
01:49:24.260 --> 01:49:26.054
What should I say?

1349
01:49:27.763 --> 01:49:29.599
Anything.

1350
01:49:31.559 --> 01:49:36.731
"Thank you for being born."
You know, that kind of thing.

1351
01:49:39.150 --> 01:49:40.902
He won't even understand.

1352
01:49:40.986 --> 01:49:42.778
Even so,

1353
01:49:43.571 --> 01:49:47.033
just once in his life...

1354
01:49:49.911 --> 01:49:51.412
Shit.

1355
01:49:57.710 --> 01:50:02.048
So-young, then say it to all of us.

1356
01:50:02.883 --> 01:50:04.759
- All of you?
- Yeah.

1357
01:50:05.343 --> 01:50:06.594
All four of you?

1358
01:50:06.677 --> 01:50:07.971
Yeah.

1359
01:50:08.263 --> 01:50:10.015
That dummy.

1360
01:50:10.390 --> 01:50:12.183
I'll pass.

1361
01:50:12.475 --> 01:50:15.186
Hey, you're the one who suggested it.

1362
01:50:17.563 --> 01:50:19.649
Then I'll pass, too.

1363
01:50:27.740 --> 01:50:29.951
All right, I'll say it.

1364
01:50:32.662 --> 01:50:35.165
Everyone close your eyes then.

1365
01:50:36.124 --> 01:50:37.708
Hold on!

1366
01:50:39.669 --> 01:50:41.337
Let's turn out the light.

1367
01:50:42.213 --> 01:50:44.465
What?

1368
01:50:44.674 --> 01:50:46.801
Then how will I eat the steak?

1369
01:50:46.885 --> 01:50:49.595
Hey! Don't turn it out.

1370
01:50:50.388 --> 01:50:52.223
Don't turn it out.

1371
01:50:55.977 --> 01:50:58.188
Okay, here we go.

1372
01:51:03.359 --> 01:51:07.864
Hae-jin, thank you for being born.

1373
01:51:12.452 --> 01:51:14.079
Sang-hyun,

1374
01:51:16.706 --> 01:51:18.917
thank you for being born.

1375
01:51:21.794 --> 01:51:23.379
Dong-soo,

1376
01:51:26.507 --> 01:51:28.551
thank you for being born.

1377
01:51:33.389 --> 01:51:35.016
Woo-sung,

1378
01:51:38.394 --> 01:51:40.146
thank you...

1379
01:51:43.108 --> 01:51:44.609
for being born.

1380
01:51:47.237 --> 01:51:48.821
So-young...

1381
01:51:53.076 --> 01:51:55.871
Thank you for being born.

1382
01:52:07.757 --> 01:52:10.676
Okay, good night everyone.

1383
01:52:12.220 --> 01:52:13.846
Good night.

1384
01:52:53.803 --> 01:52:56.014
I've got a proposition.

1385
01:53:01.686 --> 01:53:04.397
We'll say you turned yourself in here.

1386
01:53:05.815 --> 01:53:07.192
What?

1387
01:53:07.525 --> 01:53:10.862
No need to sell Woo-sung now.

1388
01:53:12.030 --> 01:53:15.116
You say to sell him,
and now you say don't?

1389
01:53:15.366 --> 01:53:21.164
Confess to accidental manslaughter,
and you can be out in 3 years.

1390
01:53:22.415 --> 01:53:26.127
Then someday you can
live with Woo-sung again.

1391
01:53:29.630 --> 01:53:34.677
Those two people can never
become parents, unfortunately.

1392
01:53:36.804 --> 01:53:38.723
Neither can I.

1393
01:53:40.600 --> 01:53:43.311
The couple we met today said,

1394
01:53:45.521 --> 01:53:48.984
Woo-sung wasn't
abandoned, he was protected.

1395
01:53:49.901 --> 01:53:53.196
That they'll tell him that every day.

1396
01:53:55.573 --> 01:53:59.077
I want him to be raised
by people like them.

1397
01:54:03.039 --> 01:54:04.916
If so,

1398
01:54:10.630 --> 01:54:12.340
If so,

1399
01:54:14.634 --> 01:54:17.470
he won't have to live like me.

1400
01:54:39.492 --> 01:54:41.369
Where are you going?

1401
01:54:44.956 --> 01:54:46.917
So-young's gone, too.

1402
01:54:47.250 --> 01:54:51.421
So-young's probably
outside with the police.

1403
01:54:53.673 --> 01:54:56.051
So-young wouldn't sell us out.

1404
01:54:56.134 --> 01:54:58.553
Yes, she would.

1405
01:54:59.304 --> 01:55:02.765
She'd do anything for Woo-sung.

1406
01:55:04.267 --> 01:55:08.146
But that's okay.

1407
01:55:13.443 --> 01:55:17.906
When you're a parent,
you'll understand.

1408
01:55:21.910 --> 01:55:24.037
If she sells us out,

1409
01:55:25.872 --> 01:55:28.541
can she start over again?

1410
01:55:30.251 --> 01:55:32.087
Sure.

1411
01:55:32.462 --> 01:55:36.883
Maybe even with Woo-sung.

1412
01:55:56.277 --> 01:55:58.738
You go first, I'll join you soon.

1413
01:56:02.283 --> 01:56:04.285
Hey, come here.

1414
01:56:04.369 --> 01:56:05.328
Look, Tae-ho.

1415
01:56:05.411 --> 01:56:06.079
I said come here!

1416
01:56:06.162 --> 01:56:07.372
- Listen to me for a sec.
- Hey, you!

1417
01:56:07.455 --> 01:56:08.706
- Listen.
- Let go!

1418
01:56:08.789 --> 01:56:11.042
You haven't given up yet?

1419
01:56:11.126 --> 01:56:12.878
Of course not!

1420
01:56:14.295 --> 01:56:16.381
Just think about it.

1421
01:56:16.797 --> 01:56:18.841
If that woman raises him,

1422
01:56:19.009 --> 01:56:22.470
how will he grow up? Will he be happy?

1423
01:56:23.013 --> 01:56:25.140
What the hell's come over you?

1424
01:56:25.265 --> 01:56:26.641
You're just a damn broker.

1425
01:56:26.724 --> 01:56:29.685
Let go of me! Shit!

1426
01:56:29.769 --> 01:56:31.354
Listen to me.

1427
01:56:31.604 --> 01:56:33.314
Instead of this,

1428
01:56:36.276 --> 01:56:39.487
let's take that 40 million
and work together.

1429
01:56:42.365 --> 01:56:45.618
You're talking nonsense! Why should I?

1430
01:56:48.371 --> 01:56:50.957
I'm not going to work
with Dong-soo anymore.

1431
01:56:54.419 --> 01:56:55.962
What?

1432
01:56:57.130 --> 01:56:59.049
Those guys,

1433
01:57:02.302 --> 01:57:05.055
they don't need me anymore.

1434
01:57:11.978 --> 01:57:15.565
My wife got really mad at
me for saying that yesterday.

1435
01:57:16.107 --> 01:57:20.862
To ask that all of a
sudden isn't fair to her.

1436
01:57:21.404 --> 01:57:25.951
So please tell his mother,
whenever she wants to see him,

1437
01:57:26.076 --> 01:57:28.578
she can call us anytime.

1438
01:57:29.579 --> 01:57:33.458
We don't want to hide
anything from the child.

1439
01:57:35.961 --> 01:57:38.046
It would've been nice

1440
01:57:39.755 --> 01:57:45.678
to give Woo-sung to people like you.

1441
01:57:50.725 --> 01:57:52.435
Who's that?

1442
01:57:52.810 --> 01:57:54.562
Is it Sang-hyun?

1443
01:57:58.399 --> 01:57:59.943
Who are you?

1444
01:58:01.444 --> 01:58:02.988
The police.

1445
01:58:03.654 --> 01:58:05.281
What's the matter?

1446
01:58:05.365 --> 01:58:08.326
You're being charged with
illegally purchasing a child.

1447
01:58:08.409 --> 01:58:10.786
- Honey!
- Stay inside for a sec.

1448
01:58:10.912 --> 01:58:13.039
Can we talk outside?

1449
01:58:13.999 --> 01:58:17.919
Kim Dong-soo? You're arrested
for suspected child trafficking.

1450
01:58:18.211 --> 01:58:19.795
Dong-soo!

1451
01:58:26.802 --> 01:58:28.596
What about So-young?

1452
01:58:29.890 --> 01:58:31.766
She turned herself in.

1453
01:58:34.269 --> 01:58:36.062
And the other man?

1454
01:58:38.857 --> 01:58:40.358
I don't know.

1455
01:58:43.069 --> 01:58:45.196
- Take them in.
- Okay.

1456
01:58:57.417 --> 01:58:59.002
Let's go.

1457
01:59:33.578 --> 01:59:34.662
<i>For our next story,</i>

1458
01:59:34.745 --> 01:59:40.460
<i>we have new info on the body found in
a Seoul underground shopping center.</i>

1459
01:59:40.626 --> 01:59:43.629
<i>The victim, surnamed Shin,
was a gangster from Busan,</i>

1460
01:59:43.713 --> 01:59:50.011
<i>and 40 million won in cash has been
found in the victim's motel room.</i>

1461
01:59:50.136 --> 01:59:56.684
<i>Police are investigating the matter
as a potential crime or accident.</i>

1462
01:59:56.977 --> 01:59:58.186
<i>Next,</i>

1463
01:59:58.269 --> 02:00:00.105
<i>to celebrate Family Month in May,</i>

1464
02:00:00.188 --> 02:00:03.942
<i>events for families are
scheduled across the country.</i>

1465
02:00:17.538 --> 02:00:19.249
Hold on a second.

1466
02:00:20.416 --> 02:00:22.293
What are you kids doing?

1467
02:00:22.460 --> 02:00:24.587
What are you doing?

1468
02:00:38.643 --> 02:00:40.395
Woo-sung!

1469
02:00:41.062 --> 02:00:42.856
Woo-sung!

1470
02:00:49.362 --> 02:00:52.573
Did you have fun?
Want to go in the ocean?

1471
02:01:23.354 --> 02:01:26.942
<i>Ms. Moon So-young, how have you been?</i>

1472
02:01:27.984 --> 02:01:31.154
<i>I was glad to hear your
sentence was reduced,</i>

1473
02:01:31.237 --> 02:01:33.489
<i>and you've been released.</i>

1474
02:01:35.033 --> 02:01:37.285
<i>It's been 3 years that I've
been caring for Woo-sung,</i>

1475
02:01:37.368 --> 02:01:41.539
<i>as you requested that day.</i>

1476
02:01:43.374 --> 02:01:47.670
<i>On the 15th this month, for
an hour starting at 12 noon,</i>

1477
02:01:47.879 --> 02:01:51.424
<i>in the park across from Busan Sky Land,</i>

1478
02:01:51.716 --> 02:01:54.427
<i>Woo-sung and I will wait for you.</i>

1479
02:01:55.887 --> 02:01:59.975
<i>We still don't know anything
about Sang-hyun's whereabouts,</i>

1480
02:02:00.100 --> 02:02:03.436
<i>but I invited Dong-soo and Hae-jin.</i>

1481
02:02:03.728 --> 02:02:08.733
<i>Busan Sky Land</i>

1482
02:02:13.363 --> 02:02:15.949
Hae-jin, get in the van!

1483
02:02:17.075 --> 02:02:20.411
<i>Mr. Yoon and his wife are on probation,</i>

1484
02:02:20.536 --> 02:02:24.124
<i>so they're not allowed to
adopt Woo-sung as you wished,</i>

1485
02:02:24.207 --> 02:02:28.461
<i>but they sometimes
come and play with him.</i>

1486
02:02:30.421 --> 02:02:35.385
<i>If you can't come this time,
we'll gather again next month.</i>

1487
02:02:36.761 --> 02:02:41.933
<i>I hope we can all discuss
Woo-sung's future.</i>

1488
02:02:48.064 --> 02:02:49.690
<i>Thank you.</i>

1489
02:02:54.905 --> 02:02:57.073
Come again!
